\id LEV American King James Version

\ide UTF-8
\h Leviticus
\toc1 The Third Book of Moses, called Leviticus
\toc2 Leviticus
\toc3 Lev
\mt1 THE THIRD BOOK OF MOSES, CALLED LEVITICUS
\c 1
\p \v 1 And the LORD called to Moses, and spoke to him out of the tabernacle of the congregation, saying,
\v 2 Speak to the children of Israel, and say to them, If any man of you bring an offering to the LORD, you shall bring your offering of the cattle, \add even\add* of the herd, and of the flock.
\v 3 If his offering \add be\add* a burnt sacrifice of the herd, let him offer a male without blemish: he shall offer it of his own voluntary will at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation before the LORD.
\v 4 And he shall put his hand on the head of the burnt offering; and it shall be accepted for him to make atonement for him.
\v 5 And he shall kill the bullock before the LORD: and the priests, Aaron's sons, shall bring the blood, and sprinkle the blood round about on the altar that \add is by\add* the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.
\v 6 And he shall flay the burnt offering, and cut it into his pieces.
\v 7 And the sons of Aaron the priest shall put fire on the altar, and lay the wood in order on the fire:
\v 8 And the priests, Aaron's sons, shall lay the parts, the head, and the fat, in order on the wood that \add is\add* on the fire which \add is\add* on the altar:
\v 9 But his inwards and his legs shall he wash in water: and the priest shall burn all on the altar, \add to be\add* a burnt sacrifice, an offering made by fire, of a sweet smell to the LORD.
\v 10 And if his offering \add be\add* of the flocks, \add namely\add*, of the sheep, or of the goats, for a burnt sacrifice; he shall bring it a male without blemish.
\v 11 And he shall kill it on the side of the altar northward before the LORD: and the priests, Aaron's sons, shall sprinkle his blood round about on the altar.
\v 12 And he shall cut it into his pieces, with his head and his fat: and the priest shall lay them in order on the wood that \add is\add* on the fire which \add is\add* on the altar:
\v 13 But he shall wash the inwards and the legs with water: and the priest shall bring \add it\add* all, and burn \add it\add* on the altar: it \add is\add* a burnt sacrifice, an offering made by fire, of a sweet smell to the LORD.
\v 14 And if the burnt sacrifice for his offering to the LORD \add be\add* of fowls, then he shall bring his offering of turtledoves, or of young pigeons.
\v 15 And the priest shall bring it to the altar, and wring off his head, and burn \add it\add* on the altar; and the blood thereof shall be wrung out at the side of the altar:
\v 16 And he shall pluck away his crop with his feathers, and cast it beside the altar on the east part, by the place of the ashes:
\v 17 And he shall split it with the wings thereof, \add but\add* shall not divide \add it\add* asunder: and the priest shall burn it on the altar, on the wood that \add is\add* on the fire: it \add is\add* a burnt sacrifice, an offering made by fire, of a sweet smell to the LORD.
\c 2
\p \v 1 And when any will offer a meat offering to the LORD, his offering shall be \add of\add* fine flour; and he shall pour oil on it, and put frankincense thereon:
\v 2 And he shall bring it to Aaron's sons the priests: and he shall take out of there his handful of the flour thereof, and of the oil thereof, with all the frankincense thereof; and the priest shall burn the memorial of it on the altar, \add to be\add* an offering made by fire, of a sweet smell to the LORD:
\v 3 And the remnant of the meat offering \add shall be\add* Aaron's and his sons': \add it is\add* a thing most holy of the offerings of the LORD made by fire.
\v 4 And if you bring an oblation of a meat offering baked in the oven, \add it shall be\add* unleavened cakes of fine flour mingled with oil, or unleavened wafers anointed with oil.
\v 5 And if your oblation \add be\add* a meat offering \add baked\add* in a pan, it shall be \add of\add* fine flour unleavened, mingled with oil.
\v 6 You shall part it in pieces, and pour oil thereon: it \add is\add* a meat offering.
\v 7 And if your oblation \add be\add* a meat offering \add baked\add* in the frying pan, it shall be made \add of\add* fine flour with oil.
\v 8 And you shall bring the meat offering that is made of these things to the LORD: and when it is presented to the priest, he shall bring it to the altar.
\v 9 And the priest shall take from the meat offering a memorial thereof, and shall burn \add it\add* on the altar: \add it is\add* an offering made by fire, of a sweet smell to the LORD.
\v 10 And that which is left of the meat offering \add shall be\add* Aaron's and his sons': \add it is\add* a thing most holy of the offerings of the LORD made by fire.
\v 11 No meat offering, which you shall bring to the LORD, shall be made with leaven: for you shall burn no leaven, nor any honey, in any offering of the LORD made by fire.
\v 12 As for the oblation of the first fruits, you shall offer them to the LORD: but they shall not be burnt on the altar for a sweet smell.
\v 13 And every oblation of your meat offering shall you season with salt; neither shall you suffer the salt of the covenant of your God to be lacking from your meat offering: with all your offerings you shall offer salt.
\v 14 And if you offer a meat offering of your first fruits to the LORD, you shall offer for the meat offering of your first fruits green ears of corn dried by the fire, \add even\add* corn beaten out of full ears.
\v 15 And you shall put oil on it, and lay frankincense thereon: it \add is\add* a meat offering.
\v 16 And the priest shall burn the memorial of it, \add part\add* of the beaten corn thereof, and \add part\add* of the oil thereof, with all the frankincense thereof: \add it is\add* an offering made by fire to the LORD.
\c 3
\p \v 1 And if his oblation \add be\add* a sacrifice of peace offering, if he offer \add it\add* of the herd; whether \add it be\add* a male or female, he shall offer it without blemish before the LORD.
\v 2 And he shall lay his hand on the head of his offering, and kill it \add at\add* the door of the tabernacle of the congregation: and Aaron's sons the priests shall sprinkle the blood on the altar round about.
\v 3 And he shall offer of the sacrifice of the peace offering an offering made by fire to the LORD; the fat that covers the inwards, and all the fat that \add is\add* on the inwards,
\v 4 And the two kidneys, and the fat that \add is\add* on them, which \add is\add* by the flanks, and the lobe above the liver, with the kidneys, it shall he take away.
\v 5 And Aaron's sons shall burn it on the altar on the burnt sacrifice, which \add is\add* on the wood that \add is\add* on the fire: \add it is\add* an offering made by fire, of a sweet smell to the LORD.
\v 6 And if his offering for a sacrifice of peace offering to the LORD \add be\add* of the flock; male or female, he shall offer it without blemish.
\v 7 If he offer a lamb for his offering, then shall he offer it before the LORD.
\v 8 And he shall lay his hand on the head of his offering, and kill it before the tabernacle of the congregation: and Aaron's sons shall sprinkle the blood thereof round about on the altar.
\v 9 And he shall offer of the sacrifice of the peace offering an offering made by fire to the LORD; the fat thereof, \add and\add* the whole rump, it shall he take off hard by the backbone; and the fat that covers the inwards, and all the fat that \add is\add* on the inwards,
\v 10 And the two kidneys, and the fat that \add is\add* on them, which \add is\add* by the flanks, and the lobe above the liver, with the kidneys, it shall he take away.
\v 11 And the priest shall burn it on the altar: \add it is\add* the food of the offering made by fire to the LORD.
\v 12 And if his offering \add be\add* a goat, then he shall offer it before the LORD.
\v 13 And he shall lay his hand on the head of it, and kill it before the tabernacle of the congregation: and the sons of Aaron shall sprinkle the blood thereof on the altar round about.
\v 14 And he shall offer thereof his offering, \add even\add* an offering made by fire to the LORD; the fat that covers the inwards, and all the fat that \add is\add* on the inwards,
\v 15 And the two kidneys, and the fat that \add is\add* on them, which \add is\add* by the flanks, and the lobe above the liver, with the kidneys, it shall he take away.
\v 16 And the priest shall burn them on the altar: \add it is\add* the food of the offering made by fire for a sweet smell: all the fat \add is\add* the LORD's.
\v 17 \add It shall be\add* a perpetual statute for your generations throughout all your dwellings, that you eat neither fat nor blood.
\c 4
\p \v 1 And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
\v 2 Speak to the children of Israel, saying, If a soul shall sin through ignorance against any of the commandments of the LORD \add concerning things\add* which ought not to be done, and shall do against any of them:
\v 3 If the priest that is anointed do sin according to the sin of the people; then let him bring for his sin, which he has sinned, a young bullock without blemish to the LORD for a sin offering.
\v 4 And he shall bring the bullock to the door of the tabernacle of the congregation before the LORD; and shall lay his hand on the bullock's head, and kill the bullock before the LORD.
\v 5 And the priest that is anointed shall take of the bullock's blood, and bring it to the tabernacle of the congregation:
\v 6 And the priest shall dip his finger in the blood, and sprinkle of the blood seven times before the LORD, before the veil of the sanctuary.
\v 7 And the priest shall put \add some\add* of the blood on the horns of the altar of sweet incense before the LORD, which \add is\add* in the tabernacle of the congregation; and shall pour all the blood of the bullock at the bottom of the altar of the burnt offering, which \add is at\add* the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.
\v 8 And he shall take off from it all the fat of the bullock for the sin offering; the fat that covers the inwards, and all the fat that \add is\add* on the inwards,
\v 9 And the two kidneys, and the fat that \add is\add* on them, which \add is\add* by the flanks, and the lobe above the liver, with the kidneys, it shall he take away,
\v 10 As it was taken off from the bullock of the sacrifice of peace offerings: and the priest shall burn them on the altar of the burnt offering.
\v 11 And the skin of the bullock, and all his flesh, with his head, and with his legs, and his inwards, and his dung,
\v 12 Even the whole bullock shall he carry forth without the camp to a clean place, where the ashes are poured out, and burn him on the wood with fire: where the ashes are poured out shall he be burnt.
\v 13 And if the whole congregation of Israel sin through ignorance, and the thing be hid from the eyes of the assembly, and they have done \add somewhat against\add* any of the commandments of the LORD \add concerning things\add* which should not be done, and are guilty;
\v 14 When the sin, which they have sinned against it, is known, then the congregation shall offer a young bullock for the sin, and bring him before the tabernacle of the congregation.
\v 15 And the elders of the congregation shall lay their hands on the head of the bullock before the LORD: and the bullock shall be killed before the LORD.
\v 16 And the priest that is anointed shall bring of the bullock's blood to the tabernacle of the congregation:
\v 17 And the priest shall dip his finger \add in some\add* of the blood, and sprinkle \add it\add* seven times before the LORD, \add even\add* before the veil.
\v 18 And he shall put \add some\add* of the blood on the horns of the altar which \add is\add* before the LORD, that \add is\add* in the tabernacle of the congregation, and shall pour out all the blood at the bottom of the altar of the burnt offering, which \add is at\add* the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.
\v 19 And he shall take all his fat from him, and burn \add it\add* on the altar.
\v 20 And he shall do with the bullock as he did with the bullock for a sin offering, so shall he do with this: and the priest shall make an atonement for them, and it shall be forgiven them.
\v 21 And he shall carry forth the bullock without the camp, and burn him as he burned the first bullock: it \add is\add* a sin offering for the congregation.
\v 22 When a ruler has sinned, and done \add somewhat\add* through ignorance \add against\add* any of the commandments of the LORD his God \add concerning things\add* which should not be done, and is guilty;
\v 23 Or if his sin, wherein he has sinned, come to his knowledge; he shall bring his offering, a kid of the goats, a male without blemish:
\v 24 And he shall lay his hand on the head of the goat, and kill it in the place where they kill the burnt offering before the LORD: it \add is\add* a sin offering.
\v 25 And the priest shall take of the blood of the sin offering with his finger, and put \add it\add* on the horns of the altar of burnt offering, and shall pour out his blood at the bottom of the altar of burnt offering.
\v 26 And he shall burn all his fat on the altar, as the fat of the sacrifice of peace offerings: and the priest shall make an atonement for him as concerning his sin, and it shall be forgiven him.
\v 27 And if any one of the common people sin through ignorance, while he does \add somewhat against\add* any of the commandments of the LORD \add concerning things\add* which ought not to be done, and be guilty;
\v 28 Or if his sin, which he has sinned, come to his knowledge: then he shall bring his offering, a kid of the goats, a female without blemish, for his sin which he has sinned.
\v 29 And he shall lay his hand on the head of the sin offering, and slay the sin offering in the place of the burnt offering.
\v 30 And the priest shall take of the blood thereof with his finger, and put \add it\add* on the horns of the altar of burnt offering, and shall pour out all the blood thereof at the bottom of the altar.
\v 31 And he shall take away all the fat thereof, as the fat is taken away from off the sacrifice of peace offerings; and the priest shall burn \add it\add* on the altar for a sweet smell to the LORD; and the priest shall make an atonement for him, and it shall be forgiven him.
\v 32 And if he bring a lamb for a sin offering, he shall bring it a female without blemish.
\v 33 And he shall lay his hand on the head of the sin offering, and slay it for a sin offering in the place where they kill the burnt offering.
\v 34 And the priest shall take of the blood of the sin offering with his finger, and put \add it\add* on the horns of the altar of burnt offering, and shall pour out all the blood thereof at the bottom of the altar:
\v 35 And he shall take away all the fat thereof, as the fat of the lamb is taken away from the sacrifice of the peace offerings; and the priest shall burn them on the altar, according to the offerings made by fire to the LORD: and the priest shall make an atonement for his sin that he has committed, and it shall be forgiven him.
\c 5
\p \v 1 And if a soul sin, and hear the voice of swearing, and \add is\add* a witness, whether he has seen or known \add of it\add*; if he do not utter \add it\add*, then he shall bear his iniquity.
\v 2 Or if a soul touch any unclean thing, whether \add it be\add* a carcass of an unclean beast, or a carcass of unclean cattle, or the carcass of unclean creeping things, and \add if\add* it be hidden from him; he also shall be unclean, and guilty.
\v 3 Or if he touch the uncleanness of man, whatever uncleanness \add it be\add* that a man shall be defiled with, and it be hid from him; when he knows \add of it\add*, then he shall be guilty.
\v 4 Or if a soul swear, pronouncing with \add his\add* lips to do evil, or to do good, whatever \add it be\add* that a man shall pronounce with an oath, and it be hid from him; when he knows \add of it\add*, then he shall be guilty in one of these.
\v 5 And it shall be, when he shall be guilty in one of these \add things\add*, that he shall confess that he has sinned in that \add thing\add*:
\v 6 And he shall bring his trespass offering to the LORD for his sin which he has sinned, a female from the flock, a lamb or a kid of the goats, for a sin offering; and the priest shall make an atonement for him concerning his sin.
\v 7 And if he be not able to bring a lamb, then he shall bring for his trespass, which he has committed, two turtledoves, or two young pigeons, to the LORD; one for a sin offering, and the other for a burnt offering.
\v 8 And he shall bring them to the priest, who shall offer \add that\add* which \add is\add* for the sin offering first, and wring off his head from his neck, but shall not divide \add it\add* asunder:
\v 9 And he shall sprinkle of the blood of the sin offering on the side of the altar; and the rest of the blood shall be wrung out at the bottom of the altar: it \add is\add* a sin offering.
\v 10 And he shall offer the second \add for\add* a burnt offering, according to the manner: and the priest shall make an atonement for him for his sin which he has sinned, and it shall be forgiven him.
\v 11 But if he be not able to bring two turtledoves, or two young pigeons, then he that sinned shall bring for his offering the tenth part of an ephah of fine flour for a sin offering; he shall put no oil on it, neither shall he put \add any\add* frankincense thereon: for it \add is\add* a sin offering.
\v 12 Then shall he bring it to the priest, and the priest shall take his handful of it, \add even\add* a memorial thereof, and burn \add it\add* on the altar, according to the offerings made by fire to the LORD: it \add is\add* a sin offering.
\v 13 And the priest shall make an atonement for him as touching his sin that he has sinned in one of these, and it shall be forgiven him: and \add the remnant\add* shall be the priest's, as a meat offering.
\v 14 And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
\v 15 If a soul commit a trespass, and sin through ignorance, in the holy things of the LORD; then he shall bring for his trespass to the LORD a ram without blemish out of the flocks, with your estimation by shekels of silver, after the shekel of the sanctuary, for a trespass offering.
\v 16 And he shall make amends for the harm that he has done in the holy thing, and shall add the fifth part thereto, and give it to the priest: and the priest shall make an atonement for him with the ram of the trespass offering, and it shall be forgiven him.
\v 17 And if a soul sin, and commit any of these things which are forbidden to be done by the commandments of the LORD; though he knew \add it\add* not, yet is he guilty, and shall bear his iniquity.
\v 18 And he shall bring a ram without blemish out of the flock, with your estimation, for a trespass offering, to the priest: and the priest shall make an atonement for him concerning his ignorance wherein he erred and knew \add it\add* not, and it shall be forgiven him.
\v 19 It \add is\add* a trespass offering: he has certainly trespassed against the LORD.
\c 6
\p \v 1 And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
\v 2 If a soul sin, and commit a trespass against the LORD, and lie to his neighbor in that which was delivered him to keep, or in fellowship, or in a thing taken away by violence, or has deceived his neighbor;
\v 3 Or have found that which was lost, and lies concerning it, and swears falsely; in any of all these that a man does, sinning therein:
\v 4 Then it shall be, because he has sinned, and is guilty, that he shall restore that which he took violently away, or the thing which he has deceitfully gotten, or that which was delivered him to keep, or the lost thing which he found,
\v 5 Or all that about which he has sworn falsely; he shall even restore it in the principal, and shall add the fifth part more thereto, \add and\add* give it to him to whom it appertains, in the day of his trespass offering.
\v 6 And he shall bring his trespass offering to the LORD, a ram without blemish out of the flock, with your estimation, for a trespass offering, to the priest:
\v 7 And the priest shall make an atonement for him before the LORD: and it shall be forgiven him for any thing of all that he has done in trespassing therein.
\v 8 And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
\v 9 Command Aaron and his sons, saying, This \add is\add* the law of the burnt offering: It \add is\add* the burnt offering, because of the burning on the altar all night to the morning, and the fire of the altar shall be burning in it.
\v 10 And the priest shall put on his linen garment, and his linen breeches shall he put on his flesh, and take up the ashes which the fire has consumed with the burnt offering on the altar, and he shall put them beside the altar.
\v 11 And he shall put off his garments, and put on other garments, and carry forth the ashes without the camp to a clean place.
\v 12 And the fire on the altar shall be burning in it; it shall not be put out: and the priest shall burn wood on it every morning, and lay the burnt offering in order on it; and he shall burn thereon the fat of the peace offerings.
\v 13 The fire shall ever be burning on the altar; it shall never go out.
\v 14 And this \add is\add* the law of the meat offering: the sons of Aaron shall offer it before the LORD, before the altar.
\v 15 And he shall take of it his handful, of the flour of the meat offering, and of the oil thereof, and all the frankincense which \add is\add* on the meat offering, and shall burn \add it\add* on the altar \add for\add* a sweet smell, \add even\add* the memorial of it, to the LORD.
\v 16 And the remainder thereof shall Aaron and his sons eat: with unleavened bread shall it be eaten in the holy place; in the court of the tabernacle of the congregation they shall eat it.
\v 17 It shall not be baked with leaven. I have given it \add to them for\add* their portion of my offerings made by fire; it \add is\add* most holy, as \add is\add* the sin offering, and as the trespass offering.
\v 18 All the males among the children of Aaron shall eat of it. \add It shall be\add* a statute for ever in your generations concerning the offerings of the LORD made by fire: every one that touches them shall be holy.
\v 19 And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
\v 20 This \add is\add* the offering of Aaron and of his sons, which they shall offer to the LORD in the day when he is anointed; the tenth part of an ephah of fine flour for a meat offering perpetual, half of it in the morning, and half thereof at night.
\v 21 In a pan it shall be made with oil; \add and when it is\add* baked, you shall bring it in: \add and\add* the baked pieces of the meat offering shall you offer \add for\add* a sweet smell to the LORD.
\v 22 And the priest of his sons that is anointed in his stead shall offer it: \add it is\add* a statute for ever to the LORD; it shall be wholly burnt.
\v 23 For every meat offering for the priest shall be wholly burnt: it shall not be eaten.
\v 24 And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
\v 25 Speak to Aaron and to his sons, saying, This \add is\add* the law of the sin offering: In the place where the burnt offering is killed shall the sin offering be killed before the LORD: it \add is\add* most holy.
\v 26 The priest that offers it for sin shall eat it: in the holy place shall it be eaten, in the court of the tabernacle of the congregation.
\v 27 Whatever shall touch the flesh thereof shall be holy: and when there is sprinkled of the blood thereof on any garment, you shall wash that where on it was sprinkled in the holy place.
\v 28 But the earthen vessel wherein it is sodden shall be broken: and if it be sodden in a brazen pot, it shall be both scoured, and rinsed in water.
\v 29 All the males among the priests shall eat thereof: it \add is\add* most holy.
\v 30 And no sin offering, whereof \add any\add* of the blood is brought into the tabernacle of the congregation to reconcile \add with\add* in the holy \add place\add*, shall be eaten: it shall be burnt in the fire.
\c 7
\p \v 1 Likewise this \add is\add* the law of the trespass offering: it \add is\add* most holy.
\v 2 In the place where they kill the burnt offering shall they kill the trespass offering: and the blood thereof shall he sprinkle round about on the altar.
\v 3 And he shall offer of it all the fat thereof; the rump, and the fat that covers the inwards,
\v 4 And the two kidneys, and the fat that \add is\add* on them, which \add is\add* by the flanks, and the lobe \add that is\add* above the liver, with the kidneys, it shall he take away:
\v 5 And the priest shall burn them on the altar \add for\add* an offering made by fire to the LORD: it \add is\add* a trespass offering.
\v 6 Every male among the priests shall eat thereof: it shall be eaten in the holy place: it \add is\add* most holy.
\v 7 As the sin offering \add is\add*, so \add is\add* the trespass offering: \add there is\add* one law for them: the priest that makes atonement therewith shall have \add it\add*.
\v 8 And the priest that offers any man's burnt offering, \add even\add* the priest shall have to himself the skin of the burnt offering which he has offered.
\v 9 And all the meat offering that is baked in the oven, and all that is dressed in the frying pan, and in the pan, shall be the priest's that offers it.
\v 10 And every meat offering, mingled with oil, and dry, shall all the sons of Aaron have, one \add as much\add* as another.
\v 11 And this \add is\add* the law of the sacrifice of peace offerings, which he shall offer to the LORD.
\v 12 If he offer it for a thanksgiving, then he shall offer with the sacrifice of thanksgiving unleavened cakes mingled with oil, and unleavened wafers anointed with oil, and cakes mingled with oil, of fine flour, fried.
\v 13 Besides the cakes, he shall offer \add for\add* his offering leavened bread with the sacrifice of thanksgiving of his peace offerings.
\v 14 And of it he shall offer one out of the whole oblation \add for\add* an heave offering to the LORD, \add and\add* it shall be the priest's that sprinkles the blood of the peace offerings.
\v 15 And the flesh of the sacrifice of his peace offerings for thanksgiving shall be eaten the same day that it is offered; he shall not leave any of it until the morning.
\v 16 But if the sacrifice of his offering \add be\add* a vow, or a voluntary offering, it shall be eaten the same day that he offers his sacrifice: and on the morrow also the remainder of it shall be eaten:
\v 17 But the remainder of the flesh of the sacrifice on the third day shall be burnt with fire.
\v 18 And if \add any\add* of the flesh of the sacrifice of his peace offerings be eaten at all on the third day, it shall not be accepted, neither shall it be imputed to him that offers it: it shall be an abomination, and the soul that eats of it shall bear his iniquity.
\v 19 And the flesh that touches any unclean \add thing\add* shall not be eaten; it shall be burnt with fire: and as for the flesh, all that be clean shall eat thereof.
\v 20 But the soul that eats \add of\add* the flesh of the sacrifice of peace offerings, that \add pertain\add* to the LORD, having his uncleanness on him, even that soul shall be cut off from his people.
\v 21 Moreover the soul that shall touch any unclean \add thing\add*, \add as\add* the uncleanness of man, or \add any\add* unclean beast, or any abominable unclean \add thing\add*, and eat of the flesh of the sacrifice of peace offerings, which \add pertain\add* to the LORD, even that soul shall be cut off from his people.
\v 22 And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
\v 23 Speak to the children of Israel, saying, You shall eat no manner of fat, of ox, or of sheep, or of goat.
\v 24 And the fat of the beast that dies of itself, and the fat of that which is torn with beasts, may be used in any other use: but you shall in no wise eat of it.
\v 25 For whoever eats the fat of the beast, of which men offer an offering made by fire to the LORD, even the soul that eats \add it\add* shall be cut off from his people.
\v 26 Moreover you shall eat no manner of blood, \add whether it be\add* of fowl or of beast, in any of your dwellings.
\v 27 Whatever soul \add it be\add* that eats any manner of blood, even that soul shall be cut off from his people.
\v 28 And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
\v 29 Speak to the children of Israel, saying, He that offers the sacrifice of his peace offerings to the LORD shall bring his oblation to the LORD of the sacrifice of his peace offerings.
\v 30 His own hands shall bring the offerings of the LORD made by fire, the fat with the breast, it shall he bring, that the breast may be waved \add for\add* a wave offering before the LORD.
\v 31 And the priest shall burn the fat on the altar: but the breast shall be Aaron's and his sons'.
\v 32 And the right shoulder shall you give to the priest \add for\add* an heave offering of the sacrifices of your peace offerings.
\v 33 He among the sons of Aaron, that offers the blood of the peace offerings, and the fat, shall have the right shoulder for \add his\add* part.
\v 34 For the wave breast and the heave shoulder have I taken of the children of Israel from off the sacrifices of their peace offerings, and have given them to Aaron the priest and to his sons by a statute for ever from among the children of Israel.
\v 35 This \add is the portion\add* of the anointing of Aaron, and of the anointing of his sons, out of the offerings of the LORD made by fire, in the day \add when\add* he presented them to minister to the LORD in the priest's office;
\v 36 Which the LORD commanded to be given them of the children of Israel, in the day that he anointed them, \add by\add* a statute for ever throughout their generations.
\v 37 This \add is\add* the law of the burnt offering, of the meat offering, and of the sin offering, and of the trespass offering, and of the consecrations, and of the sacrifice of the peace offerings;
\v 38 Which the LORD commanded Moses in mount Sinai, in the day that he commanded the children of Israel to offer their oblations to the LORD, in the wilderness of Sinai.
\c 8
\p \v 1 And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
\v 2 Take Aaron and his sons with him, and the garments, and the anointing oil, and a bullock for the sin offering, and two rams, and a basket of unleavened bread;
\v 3 And gather you all the congregation together to the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.
\v 4 And Moses did as the LORD commanded him; and the assembly was gathered together to the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.
\v 5 And Moses said to the congregation, This \add is\add* the thing which the LORD commanded to be done.
\v 6 And Moses brought Aaron and his sons, and washed them with water.
\v 7 And he put on him the coat, and girded him with the girdle, and clothed him with the robe, and put the ephod on him, and he girded him with the curious girdle of the ephod, and bound \add it\add* to him therewith.
\v 8 And he put the breastplate on him: also he put in the breastplate the Urim and the Thummim.
\v 9 And he put the turban on his head; also on the turban, \add even\add* on his forefront, did he put the golden plate, the holy crown; as the LORD commanded Moses.
\v 10 And Moses took the anointing oil, and anointed the tabernacle and all that \add was\add* therein, and sanctified them.
\v 11 And he sprinkled thereof on the altar seven times, and anointed the altar and all his vessels, both the laver and his foot, to sanctify them.
\v 12 And he poured of the anointing oil on Aaron's head, and anointed him, to sanctify him.
\v 13 And Moses brought Aaron's sons, and put coats on them, and girded them with girdles, and put bonnets on them; as the LORD commanded Moses.
\v 14 And he brought the bullock for the sin offering: and Aaron and his sons laid their hands on the head of the bullock for the sin offering.
\v 15 And he slew \add it\add*; and Moses took the blood, and put \add it\add* on the horns of the altar round about with his finger, and purified the altar, and poured the blood at the bottom of the altar, and sanctified it, to make reconciliation on it.
\v 16 And he took all the fat that \add was\add* on the inwards, and the lobe \add above\add* the liver, and the two kidneys, and their fat, and Moses burned \add it\add* on the altar.
\v 17 But the bullock, and his hide, his flesh, and his dung, he burnt with fire without the camp; as the LORD commanded Moses.
\v 18 And he brought the ram for the burnt offering: and Aaron and his sons laid their hands on the head of the ram.
\v 19 And he killed \add it\add*; and Moses sprinkled the blood on the altar round about.
\v 20 And he cut the ram into pieces; and Moses burnt the head, and the pieces, and the fat.
\v 21 And he washed the inwards and the legs in water; and Moses burnt the whole ram on the altar: it \add was\add* a burnt sacrifice for a sweet smell, \add and\add* an offering made by fire to the LORD; as the LORD commanded Moses.
\v 22 And he brought the other ram, the ram of consecration: and Aaron and his sons laid their hands on the head of the ram.
\v 23 And he slew \add it\add*; and Moses took of the blood of it, and put \add it\add* on the tip of Aaron's right ear, and on the thumb of his right hand, and on the great toe of his right foot.
\v 24 And he brought Aaron's sons, and Moses put of the blood on the tip of their right ear, and on the thumbs of their right hands, and on the great toes of their right feet: and Moses sprinkled the blood on the altar round about.
\v 25 And he took the fat, and the rump, and all the fat that \add was\add* on the inwards, and the lobe \add above\add* the liver, and the two kidneys, and their fat, and the right shoulder:
\v 26 And out of the basket of unleavened bread, that \add was\add* before the LORD, he took one unleavened cake, and a cake of oiled bread, and one wafer, and put \add them\add* on the fat, and on the right shoulder:
\v 27 And he put all on Aaron's hands, and on his sons' hands, and waved them \add for\add* a wave offering before the LORD.
\v 28 And Moses took them from off their hands, and burnt \add them\add* on the altar on the burnt offering: they \add were\add* consecrations for a sweet smell: it \add is\add* an offering made by fire to the LORD.
\v 29 And Moses took the breast, and waved it \add for\add* a wave offering before the LORD: \add for\add* of the ram of consecration it was Moses' part; as the LORD commanded Moses.
\v 30 And Moses took of the anointing oil, and of the blood which \add was\add* on the altar, and sprinkled \add it\add* on Aaron, \add and\add* on his garments, and on his sons, and on his sons' garments with him; and sanctified Aaron, \add and\add* his garments, and his sons, and his sons' garments with him.
\v 31 And Moses said to Aaron and to his sons, Boil the flesh \add at\add* the door of the tabernacle of the congregation: and there eat it with the bread that \add is\add* in the basket of consecrations, as I commanded, saying, Aaron and his sons shall eat it.
\v 32 And that which remains of the flesh and of the bread shall you burn with fire.
\v 33 And you shall not go out of the door of the tabernacle of the congregation \add in\add* seven days, until the days of your consecration be at an end: for seven days shall he consecrate you.
\v 34 As he has done this day, \add so\add* the LORD has commanded to do, to make an atonement for you.
\v 35 Therefore shall you abide \add at\add* the door of the tabernacle of the congregation day and night seven days, and keep the charge of the LORD, that you die not: for so I am commanded.
\v 36 So Aaron and his sons did all things which the LORD commanded by the hand of Moses.
\c 9
\p \v 1 And it came to pass on the eighth day, \add that\add* Moses called Aaron and his sons, and the elders of Israel;
\v 2 And he said to Aaron, Take you a young calf for a sin offering, and a ram for a burnt offering, without blemish, and offer \add them\add* before the LORD.
\v 3 And to the children of Israel you shall speak, saying, Take you a kid of the goats for a sin offering; and a calf and a lamb, \add both\add* of the first year, without blemish, for a burnt offering;
\v 4 Also a bullock and a ram for peace offerings, to sacrifice before the LORD; and a meat offering mingled with oil: for to day the LORD will appear to you.
\v 5 And they brought \add that\add* which Moses commanded before the tabernacle of the congregation: and all the congregation drew near and stood before the LORD.
\v 6 And Moses said, This \add is\add* the thing which the LORD commanded that you should do: and the glory of the LORD shall appear to you.
\v 7 And Moses said to Aaron, Go to the altar, and offer your sin offering, and your burnt offering, and make an atonement for yourself, and for the people: and offer the offering of the people, and make an atonement for them; as the LORD commanded.
\v 8 Aaron therefore went to the altar, and slew the calf of the sin offering, which \add was\add* for himself.
\v 9 And the sons of Aaron brought the blood to him: and he dipped his finger in the blood, and put \add it\add* on the horns of the altar, and poured out the blood at the bottom of the altar:
\v 10 But the fat, and the kidneys, and the lobe above the liver of the sin offering, he burnt on the altar; as the LORD commanded Moses.
\v 11 And the flesh and the hide he burnt with fire without the camp.
\v 12 And he slew the burnt offering; and Aaron's sons presented to him the blood, which he sprinkled round about on the altar.
\v 13 And they presented the burnt offering to him, with the pieces thereof, and the head: and he burnt \add them\add* on the altar.
\v 14 And he did wash the inwards and the legs, and burnt \add them\add* on the burnt offering on the altar.
\v 15 And he brought the people's offering, and took the goat, which \add was\add* the sin offering for the people, and slew it, and offered it for sin, as the first.
\v 16 And he brought the burnt offering, and offered it according to the manner.
\v 17 And he brought the meat offering, and took an handful thereof, and burnt \add it\add* on the altar, beside the burnt sacrifice of the morning.
\v 18 He slew also the bullock and the ram \add for\add* a sacrifice of peace offerings, which \add was\add* for the people: and Aaron's sons presented to him the blood, which he sprinkled on the altar round about,
\v 19 And the fat of the bullock and of the ram, the rump, and that which covers \add the inwards\add*, and the kidneys, and the lobe \add above\add* the liver:
\v 20 And they put the fat on the breasts, and he burnt the fat on the altar:
\v 21 And the breasts and the right shoulder Aaron waved \add for\add* a wave offering before the LORD; as Moses commanded.
\v 22 And Aaron lifted up his hand toward the people, and blessed them, and came down from offering of the sin offering, and the burnt offering, and peace offerings.
\v 23 And Moses and Aaron went into the tabernacle of the congregation, and came out, and blessed the people: and the glory of the LORD appeared to all the people.
\v 24 And there came a fire out from before the LORD, and consumed on the altar the burnt offering and the fat: \add which\add* when all the people saw, they shouted, and fell on their faces.
\c 10
\p \v 1 And Nadab and Abihu, the sons of Aaron, took either of them his censer, and put fire therein, and put incense thereon, and offered strange fire before the LORD, which he commanded them not.
\v 2 And there went out fire from the LORD, and devoured them, and they died before the LORD.
\v 3 Then Moses said to Aaron, This \add is it\add* that the LORD spoke, saying, I will be sanctified in them that come near me, and before all the people I will be glorified. And Aaron held his peace.
\v 4 And Moses called Mishael and Elzaphan, the sons of Uzziel the uncle of Aaron, and said to them, Come near, carry your brothers from before the sanctuary out of the camp.
\v 5 So they went near, and carried them in their coats out of the camp; as Moses had said.
\v 6 And Moses said to Aaron, and to Eleazar and to Ithamar, his sons, Uncover not your heads, neither rend your clothes; lest you die, and lest wrath come on all the people: but let your brothers, the whole house of Israel, mourn the burning which the LORD has kindled.
\v 7 And you shall not go out from the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, lest you die: for the anointing oil of the LORD \add is\add* on you. And they did according to the word of Moses.
\v 8 And the LORD spoke to Aaron, saying,
\v 9 Do not drink wine nor strong drink, you, nor your sons with you, when you go into the tabernacle of the congregation, lest you die: \add it shall be\add* a statute for ever throughout your generations:
\v 10 And that you may put difference between holy and unholy, and between unclean and clean;
\v 11 And that you may teach the children of Israel all the statutes which the LORD has spoken to them by the hand of Moses.
\v 12 And Moses spoke to Aaron, and to Eleazar and to Ithamar, his sons that were left, Take the meat offering that remains of the offerings of the LORD made by fire, and eat it without leaven beside the altar: for it \add is\add* most holy:
\v 13 And you shall eat it in the holy place, because it \add is\add* your due, and your sons' due, of the sacrifices of the LORD made by fire: for so I am commanded.
\v 14 And the wave breast and heave shoulder shall you eat in a clean place; you, and your sons, and your daughters with you: for \add they be\add* your due, and your sons' due, \add which\add* are given out of the sacrifices of peace offerings of the children of Israel.
\v 15 The heave shoulder and the wave breast shall they bring with the offerings made by fire of the fat, to wave \add it for\add* a wave offering before the LORD; and it shall be yours, and your sons' with you, by a statute for ever; as the LORD has commanded.
\v 16 And Moses diligently sought the goat of the sin offering, and, behold, it was burnt: and he was angry with Eleazar and Ithamar, the sons of Aaron \add which were\add* left \add alive\add*, saying,
\v 17 Why have you not eaten the sin offering in the holy place, seeing it \add is\add* most holy, and \add God\add* has given it you to bear the iniquity of the congregation, to make atonement for them before the LORD?
\v 18 Behold, the blood of it was not brought in within the holy \add place\add*: you should indeed have eaten it in the holy \add place\add*, as I commanded.
\v 19 And Aaron said to Moses, Behold, this day have they offered their sin offering and their burnt offering before the LORD; and such things have befallen me: and \add if\add* I had eaten the sin offering to day, should it have been accepted in the sight of the LORD?
\v 20 And when Moses heard \add that\add*, he was content.
\c 11
\p \v 1 And the LORD spoke to Moses and to Aaron, saying to them,
\v 2 Speak to the children of Israel, saying, These \add are\add* the beasts which you shall eat among all the beasts that \add are\add* on the earth.
\v 3 Whatever parts the hoof, and is cloven footed, \add and\add* chews the cud, among the beasts, that shall you eat.
\v 4 Nevertheless these shall you not eat of them that chew the cud, or of them that divide the hoof: \add as\add* the camel, because he chews the cud, but divides not the hoof; he \add is\add* unclean to you.
\v 5 And the coney, because he chews the cud, but divides not the hoof; he \add is\add* unclean to you.
\v 6 And the hare, because he chews the cud, but divides not the hoof; he \add is\add* unclean to you.
\v 7 And the swine, though he divide the hoof, and be cloven footed, yet he chews not the cud; he \add is\add* unclean to you.
\v 8 Of their flesh shall you not eat, and their carcass shall you not touch; they \add are\add* unclean to you.
\v 9 These shall you eat of all that \add are\add* in the waters: whatever has fins and scales in the waters, in the seas, and in the rivers, them shall you eat.
\v 10 And all that have not fins and scales in the seas, and in the rivers, of all that move in the waters, and of any living thing which \add is\add* in the waters, they \add shall be\add* an abomination to you:
\v 11 They shall be even an abomination to you; you shall not eat of their flesh, but you shall have their carcasses in abomination.
\v 12 Whatever has no fins nor scales in the waters, that \add shall be\add* an abomination to you.
\v 13 And these \add are they which\add* you shall have in abomination among the fowls; they shall not be eaten, they \add are\add* an abomination: the eagle, and the ossifrage, and the ospray,
\v 14 And the vulture, and the kite after his kind;
\v 15 Every raven after his kind;
\v 16 And the owl, and the night hawk, and the cuckow, and the hawk after his kind,
\v 17 And the little owl, and the cormorant, and the great owl,
\v 18 And the swan, and the pelican, and the gier eagle,
\v 19 And the stork, the heron after her kind, and the lapwing, and the bat.
\v 20 All fowls that creep, going on \add all\add* four, \add shall be\add* an abomination to you.
\v 21 Yet these may you eat of every flying creeping thing that goes on \add all\add* four, which have legs above their feet, to leap with on the earth;
\v 22 \add Even\add* these of them you may eat; the locust after his kind, and the bald locust after his kind, and the beetle after his kind, and the grasshopper after his kind.
\v 23 But all \add other\add* flying creeping things, which have four feet, \add shall be\add* an abomination to you.
\v 24 And for these you shall be unclean: whoever touches the carcass of them shall be unclean until the even.
\v 25 And whoever bears \add ought\add* of the carcass of them shall wash his clothes, and be unclean until the even.
\v 26 \add The carcasses\add* of every beast which divides the hoof, and \add is\add* not cloven footed, nor chews the cud, \add are\add* unclean to you: every one that touches them shall be unclean.
\v 27 And whatever goes on his paws, among all manner of beasts that go on \add all\add* four, those \add are\add* unclean to you: whoever touches their carcass shall be unclean until the even.
\v 28 And he that bears the carcass of them shall wash his clothes, and be unclean until the even: they \add are\add* unclean to you.
\v 29 These also \add shall be\add* unclean to you among the creeping things that creep on the earth; the weasel, and the mouse, and the tortoise after his kind,
\v 30 And the ferret, and the chameleon, and the lizard, and the snail, and the mole.
\v 31 These \add are\add* unclean to you among all that creep: whoever does touch them, when they be dead, shall be unclean until the even.
\v 32 And on whatever \add any\add* of them, when they are dead, does fall, it shall be unclean; whether \add it be\add* any vessel of wood, or raiment, or skin, or sack, whatever vessel \add it be\add*, wherein \add any\add* work is done, it must be put into water, and it shall be unclean until the even; so it shall be cleansed.
\v 33 And every earthen vessel, into where \add any\add* of them falls, whatever \add is\add* in it shall be unclean; and you shall break it.
\v 34 Of all meat which may be eaten, \add that\add* on which \add such\add* water comes shall be unclean: and all drink that may be drunk in every \add such\add* vessel shall be unclean.
\v 35 And every \add thing\add* whereupon \add any part\add* of their carcass falls shall be unclean; \add whether it be\add* oven, or ranges for pots, they shall be broken down: \add for\add* they \add are\add* unclean and shall be unclean to you.
\v 36 Nevertheless a fountain or pit, \add wherein there is\add* plenty of water, shall be clean: but that which touches their carcass shall be unclean.
\v 37 And if \add any part\add* of their carcass fall on any sowing seed which is to be sown, it \add shall be\add* clean.
\v 38 But if \add any\add* water be put on the seed, and \add any part\add* of their carcass fall thereon, it \add shall be\add* unclean to you.
\v 39 And if any beast, of which you may eat, die; he that touches the carcass thereof shall be unclean until the even.
\v 40 And he that eats of the carcass of it shall wash his clothes, and be unclean until the even: he also that bears the carcass of it shall wash his clothes, and be unclean until the even.
\v 41 And every creeping thing that creeps on the earth \add shall be\add* an abomination; it shall not be eaten.
\v 42 Whatever goes on the belly, and whatever goes on \add all\add* four, or whatever has more feet among all creeping things that creep on the earth, them you shall not eat; for they \add are\add* an abomination.
\v 43 You shall not make yourselves abominable with any creeping thing that creeps, neither shall you make yourselves unclean with them, that you should be defiled thereby.
\v 44 For I \add am\add* the LORD your God: you shall therefore sanctify yourselves, and you shall be holy; for I \add am\add* holy: neither shall you defile yourselves with any manner of creeping thing that creeps on the earth.
\v 45 For I \add am\add* the LORD that brings you up out of the land of Egypt, to be your God: you shall therefore be holy, for I \add am\add* holy.
\v 46 This \add is\add* the law of the beasts, and of the fowl, and of every living creature that moves in the waters, and of every creature that creeps on the earth:
\v 47 To make a difference between the unclean and the clean, and between the beast that may be eaten and the beast that may not be eaten.
\c 12
\p \v 1 And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
\v 2 Speak to the children of Israel, saying, If a woman have conceived seed, and born a man child: then she shall be unclean seven days; according to the days of the separation for her infirmity shall she be unclean.
\v 3 And in the eighth day the flesh of his foreskin shall be circumcised.
\v 4 And she shall then continue in the blood of her purifying three and thirty days; she shall touch no hallowed thing, nor come into the sanctuary, until the days of her purifying be fulfilled.
\v 5 But if she bear a maid child, then she shall be unclean two weeks, as in her separation: and she shall continue in the blood of her purifying three score and six days.
\v 6 And when the days of her purifying are fulfilled, for a son, or for a daughter, she shall bring a lamb of the first year for a burnt offering, and a young pigeon, or a turtledove, for a sin offering, to the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, to the priest:
\v 7 Who shall offer it before the LORD, and make an atonement for her; and she shall be cleansed from the issue of her blood. This \add is\add* the law for her that has born a male or a female.
\v 8 And if she be not able to bring a lamb, then she shall bring two turtles, or two young pigeons; the one for the burnt offering, and the other for a sin offering: and the priest shall make an atonement for her, and she shall be clean.
\c 13
\p \v 1 And the LORD spoke to Moses and Aaron, saying,
\v 2 When a man shall have in the skin of his flesh a rising, a scab, or bright spot, and it be in the skin of his flesh \add like\add* the plague of leprosy; then he shall be brought to Aaron the priest, or to one of his sons the priests:
\v 3 And the priest shall look on the plague in the skin of the flesh: and \add when\add* the hair in the plague is turned white, and the plague in sight \add be\add* deeper than the skin of his flesh, it \add is\add* a plague of leprosy: and the priest shall look on him, and pronounce him unclean.
\v 4 If the bright spot \add be\add* white in the skin of his flesh, and in sight \add be\add* not deeper than the skin, and the hair thereof be not turned white; then the priest shall shut up \add him that has\add* the plague seven days:
\v 5 And the priest shall look on him the seventh day: and, behold, \add if\add* the plague in his sight be at a stay, \add and\add* the plague spread not in the skin; then the priest shall shut him up seven days more:
\v 6 And the priest shall look on him again the seventh day: and, behold, \add if\add* the plague \add be\add* somewhat dark, \add and\add* the plague spread not in the skin, the priest shall pronounce him clean: it \add is but\add* a scab: and he shall wash his clothes, and be clean.
\v 7 But if the scab spread much abroad in the skin, after that he has been seen of the priest for his cleansing, he shall be seen of the priest again.
\v 8 And \add if\add* the priest see that, behold, the scab spreads in the skin, then the priest shall pronounce him unclean: it \add is\add* a leprosy.
\v 9 When the plague of leprosy is in a man, then he shall be brought to the priest;
\v 10 And the priest shall see \add him\add*: and, behold, \add if\add* the rising \add be\add* white in the skin, and it have turned the hair white, and \add there be\add* quick raw flesh in the rising;
\v 11 It \add is\add* an old leprosy in the skin of his flesh, and the priest shall pronounce him unclean, and shall not shut him up: for he \add is\add* unclean.
\v 12 And if a leprosy break out abroad in the skin, and the leprosy cover all the skin of \add him that has\add* the plague from his head even to his foot, wherever the priest looks;
\v 13 Then the priest shall consider: and, behold, \add if\add* the leprosy have covered all his flesh, he shall pronounce \add him\add* clean \add that has\add* the plague: it is all turned white: he \add is\add* clean.
\v 14 But when raw flesh appears in him, he shall be unclean.
\v 15 And the priest shall see the raw flesh, and pronounce him to be unclean: \add for\add* the raw flesh \add is\add* unclean: it \add is\add* a leprosy.
\v 16 Or if the raw flesh turn again, and be changed to white, he shall come to the priest;
\v 17 And the priest shall see him: and, behold, \add if\add* the plague be turned into white; then the priest shall pronounce \add him\add* clean \add that has\add* the plague: he \add is\add* clean.
\v 18 The flesh also, in which, \add even\add* in the skin thereof, was a boil, and is healed,
\v 19 And in the place of the boil there be a white rising, or a bright spot, white, and somewhat reddish, and it be showed to the priest;
\v 20 And if, when the priest sees it, behold, it \add be\add* in sight lower than the skin, and the hair thereof be turned white; the priest shall pronounce him unclean: it \add is\add* a plague of leprosy broken out of the boil.
\v 21 But if the priest look on it, and, behold, \add there be\add* no white hairs therein, and \add if\add* it \add be\add* not lower than the skin, but \add be\add* somewhat dark; then the priest shall shut him up seven days:
\v 22 And if it spread much abroad in the skin, then the priest shall pronounce him unclean: it \add is\add* a plague.
\v 23 But if the bright spot stay in his place, \add and\add* spread not, it \add is\add* a burning boil; and the priest shall pronounce him clean.
\v 24 Or if there be \add any\add* flesh, in the skin whereof \add there is\add* a hot burning, and the quick \add flesh\add* that burns have a white bright spot, somewhat reddish, or white;
\v 25 Then the priest shall look on it: and, behold, \add if\add* the hair in the bright spot be turned white, and it \add be in\add* sight deeper than the skin; it \add is\add* a leprosy broken out of the burning: why the priest shall pronounce him unclean: it \add is\add* the plague of leprosy.
\v 26 But if the priest look on it, and, behold, \add there be\add* no white hair in the bright spot, and it \add be\add* no lower than the \add other\add* skin, but \add be\add* somewhat dark; then the priest shall shut him up seven days:
\v 27 And the priest shall look on him the seventh day: \add and\add* if it be spread much abroad in the skin, then the priest shall pronounce him unclean: it \add is\add* the plague of leprosy.
\v 28 And if the bright spot stay in his place, \add and\add* spread not in the skin, but it \add be\add* somewhat dark; it \add is\add* a rising of the burning, and the priest shall pronounce him clean: for it \add is\add* an inflammation of the burning.
\v 29 If a man or woman have a plague on the head or the beard;
\v 30 Then the priest shall see the plague: and, behold, if it \add be\add* in sight deeper than the skin; \add and there be\add* in it a yellow thin hair; then the priest shall pronounce him unclean: it \add is\add* a dry scale, \add even\add* a leprosy on the head or beard.
\v 31 And if the priest look on the plague of the scale, and, behold, it \add be\add* not in sight deeper than the skin, and \add that there is\add* no black hair in it; then the priest shall shut up \add him that has\add* the plague of the scale seven days:
\v 32 And in the seventh day the priest shall look on the plague: and, behold, \add if\add* the scale spread not, and there be in it no yellow hair, and the scale \add be\add* not in sight deeper than the skin;
\v 33 He shall be shaven, but the scale shall he not shave; and the priest shall shut up \add him that has\add* the scale seven days more:
\v 34 And in the seventh day the priest shall look on the scale: and, behold, \add if\add* the scale be not spread in the skin, nor \add be\add* in sight deeper than the skin; then the priest shall pronounce him clean: and he shall wash his clothes, and be clean.
\v 35 But if the scale spread much in the skin after his cleansing;
\v 36 Then the priest shall look on him: and, behold, if the scale be spread in the skin, the priest shall not seek for yellow hair; he \add is\add* unclean.
\v 37 But if the scale be in his sight at a stay, and \add that\add* there is black hair grown up therein; the scale is healed, he \add is\add* clean: and the priest shall pronounce him clean.
\v 38 If a man also or a woman have in the skin of their flesh bright spots, \add even\add* white bright spots;
\v 39 Then the priest shall look: and, behold, \add if\add* the bright spots in the skin of their flesh \add be\add* darkish white; it \add is\add* a freckled spot \add that\add* grows in the skin; he \add is\add* clean.
\v 40 And the man whose hair is fallen off his head, he \add is\add* bald; \add yet is\add* he clean.
\v 41 And he that has his hair fallen off from the part of his head toward his face, he \add is\add* forehead bald: \add yet is\add* he clean.
\v 42 And if there be in the bald head, or bald forehead, a white reddish sore; it \add is\add* a leprosy sprung up in his bald head, or his bald forehead.
\v 43 Then the priest shall look on it: and, behold, \add if\add* the rising of the sore \add be\add* white reddish in his bald head, or in his bald forehead, as the leprosy appears in the skin of the flesh;
\v 44 He is a leprous man, he \add is\add* unclean: the priest shall pronounce him utterly unclean; his plague \add is\add* in his head.
\v 45 And the leper in whom the plague \add is\add*, his clothes shall be rent, and his head bore, and he shall put a covering on his upper lip, and shall cry, Unclean, unclean.
\v 46 All the days wherein the plague \add shall be\add* in him he shall be defiled; he \add is\add* unclean: he shall dwell alone; without the camp \add shall\add* his habitation \add be\add*.
\v 47 The garment also that the plague of leprosy is in, \add whether it be\add* a woolen garment, or a linen garment;
\v 48 Whether \add it be\add* in the warp, or woof; of linen, or of woolen; whether in a skin, or in any thing made of skin;
\v 49 And if the plague be greenish or reddish in the garment, or in the skin, either in the warp, or in the woof, or in any thing of skin; it \add is\add* a plague of leprosy, and shall be showed to the priest:
\v 50 And the priest shall look on the plague, and shut up \add it that has\add* the plague seven days:
\v 51 And he shall look on the plague on the seventh day: if the plague be spread in the garment, either in the warp, or in the woof, or in a skin, \add or\add* in any work that is made of skin; the plague \add is\add* a fretting leprosy; it \add is\add* unclean.
\v 52 He shall therefore burn that garment, whether warp or woof, in woolen or in linen, or any thing of skin, wherein the plague is: for it \add is\add* a fretting leprosy; it shall be burnt in the fire.
\v 53 And if the priest shall look, and, behold, the plague be not spread in the garment, either in the warp, or in the woof, or in any thing of skin;
\v 54 Then the priest shall command that they wash \add the thing\add* wherein the plague \add is\add*, and he shall shut it up seven days more:
\v 55 And the priest shall look on the plague, after that it is washed: and, behold, \add if\add* the plague have not changed his color, and the plague be not spread; it \add is\add* unclean; you shall burn it in the fire; it \add is\add* fret inward, \add whether\add* it \add be\add* bore within or without.
\v 56 And if the priest look, and, behold, the plague \add be\add* somewhat dark after the washing of it; then he shall rend it out of the garment, or out of the skin, or out of the warp, or out of the woof:
\v 57 And if it appear still in the garment, either in the warp, or in the woof, or in any thing of skin; it \add is\add* a spreading \add plague\add*: you shall burn that wherein the plague \add is\add* with fire.
\v 58 And the garment, either warp, or woof, or whatever thing of skin \add it be\add*, which you shall wash, if the plague be departed from them, then it shall be washed the second time, and shall be clean.
\v 59 This \add is\add* the law of the plague of leprosy in a garment of woolen or linen, either in the warp, or woof, or any thing of skins, to pronounce it clean, or to pronounce it unclean.
\c 14
\p \v 1 And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
\v 2 This shall be the law of the leper in the day of his cleansing: He shall be brought to the priest:
\v 3 And the priest shall go forth out of the camp; and the priest shall look, and, behold, \add if\add* the plague of leprosy be healed in the leper;
\v 4 Then shall the priest command to take for him that is to be cleansed two birds alive \add and\add* clean, and cedar wood, and scarlet, and hyssop:
\v 5 And the priest shall command that one of the birds be killed in an earthen vessel over running water:
\v 6 As for the living bird, he shall take it, and the cedar wood, and the scarlet, and the hyssop, and shall dip them and the living bird in the blood of the bird \add that was\add* killed over the running water:
\v 7 And he shall sprinkle on him that is to be cleansed from the leprosy seven times, and shall pronounce him clean, and shall let the living bird loose into the open field.
\v 8 And he that is to be cleansed shall wash his clothes, and shave off all his hair, and wash himself in water, that he may be clean: and after that he shall come into the camp, and shall tarry abroad out of his tent seven days.
\v 9 But it shall be on the seventh day, that he shall shave all his hair off his head and his beard and his eyebrows, even all his hair he shall shave off: and he shall wash his clothes, also he shall wash his flesh in water, and he shall be clean.
\v 10 And on the eighth day he shall take two he lambs without blemish, and one ewe lamb of the first year without blemish, and three tenth deals of fine flour \add for\add* a meat offering, mingled with oil, and one log of oil.
\v 11 And the priest that makes \add him\add* clean shall present the man that is to be made clean, and those things, before the LORD, \add at\add* the door of the tabernacle of the congregation:
\v 12 And the priest shall take one he lamb, and offer him for a trespass offering, and the log of oil, and wave them \add for\add* a wave offering before the LORD:
\v 13 And he shall slay the lamb in the place where he shall kill the sin offering and the burnt offering, in the holy place: for as the sin offering \add is\add* the priest's, \add so is\add* the trespass offering: it \add is\add* most holy:
\v 14 And the priest shall take \add some\add* of the blood of the trespass offering, and the priest shall put \add it\add* on the tip of the right ear of him that is to be cleansed, and on the thumb of his right hand, and on the great toe of his right foot:
\v 15 And the priest shall take \add some\add* of the log of oil, and pour \add it\add* into the palm of his own left hand:
\v 16 And the priest shall dip his right finger in the oil that \add is\add* in his left hand, and shall sprinkle of the oil with his finger seven times before the LORD:
\v 17 And of the rest of the oil that \add is\add* in his hand shall the priest put on the tip of the right ear of him that is to be cleansed, and on the thumb of his right hand, and on the great toe of his right foot, on the blood of the trespass offering:
\v 18 And the remnant of the oil that \add is\add* in the priest's hand he shall pour on the head of him that is to be cleansed: and the priest shall make an atonement for him before the LORD.
\v 19 And the priest shall offer the sin offering, and make an atonement for him that is to be cleansed from his uncleanness; and afterward he shall kill the burnt offering:
\v 20 And the priest shall offer the burnt offering and the meat offering on the altar: and the priest shall make an atonement for him, and he shall be clean.
\v 21 And if he \add be\add* poor, and cannot get so much; then he shall take one lamb \add for\add* a trespass offering to be waved, to make an atonement for him, and one tenth deal of fine flour mingled with oil for a meat offering, and a log of oil;
\v 22 And two turtledoves, or two young pigeons, such as he is able to get; and the one shall be a sin offering, and the other a burnt offering.
\v 23 And he shall bring them on the eighth day for his cleansing to the priest, to the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, before the LORD.
\v 24 And the priest shall take the lamb of the trespass offering, and the log of oil, and the priest shall wave them \add for\add* a wave offering before the LORD:
\v 25 And he shall kill the lamb of the trespass offering, and the priest shall take \add some\add* of the blood of the trespass offering, and put \add it\add* on the tip of the right ear of him that is to be cleansed, and on the thumb of his right hand, and on the great toe of his right foot:
\v 26 And the priest shall pour of the oil into the palm of his own left hand:
\v 27 And the priest shall sprinkle with his right finger \add some\add* of the oil that \add is\add* in his left hand seven times before the LORD:
\v 28 And the priest shall put of the oil that \add is\add* in his hand on the tip of the right ear of him that is to be cleansed, and on the thumb of his right hand, and on the great toe of his right foot, on the place of the blood of the trespass offering:
\v 29 And the rest of the oil that \add is\add* in the priest's hand he shall put on the head of him that is to be cleansed, to make an atonement for him before the LORD.
\v 30 And he shall offer the one of the turtledoves, or of the young pigeons, such as he can get;
\v 31 \add Even\add* such as he is able to get, the one \add for\add* a sin offering, and the other \add for\add* a burnt offering, with the meat offering: and the priest shall make an atonement for him that is to be cleansed before the LORD.
\v 32 This \add is\add* the law \add of him\add* in whom \add is\add* the plague of leprosy, whose hand is not able to get \add that which pertains\add* to his cleansing.
\v 33 And the LORD spoke to Moses and to Aaron, saying,
\v 34 When you be come into the land of Canaan, which I give to you for a possession, and I put the plague of leprosy in a house of the land of your possession;
\v 35 And he that ownes the house shall come and tell the priest, saying, It seems to me \add there is\add* as it were a plague in the house:
\v 36 Then the priest shall command that they empty the house, before the priest go \add into it\add* to see the plague, that all that \add is\add* in the house be not made unclean: and afterward the priest shall go in to see the house:
\v 37 And he shall look on the plague, and, behold, \add if\add* the plague \add be\add* in the walls of the house with hollow strakes, greenish or reddish, which in sight \add are\add* lower than the wall;
\v 38 Then the priest shall go out of the house to the door of the house, and shut up the house seven days:
\v 39 And the priest shall come again the seventh day, and shall look: and, behold, \add if\add* the plague be spread in the walls of the house;
\v 40 Then the priest shall command that they take away the stones in which the plague \add is\add*, and they shall cast them into an unclean place without the city:
\v 41 And he shall cause the house to be scraped within round about, and they shall pour out the dust that they scrape off without the city into an unclean place:
\v 42 And they shall take other stones, and put \add them\add* in the place of those stones; and he shall take other mortar, and shall plaster the house.
\v 43 And if the plague come again, and break out in the house, after that he has taken away the stones, and after he has scraped the house, and after it is plastered;
\v 44 Then the priest shall come and look, and, behold, \add if\add* the plague be spread in the house, it \add is\add* a fretting leprosy in the house; it \add is\add* unclean.
\v 45 And he shall break down the house, the stones of it, and the timber thereof, and all the mortar of the house; and he shall carry \add them\add* forth out of the city into an unclean place.
\v 46 Moreover he that goes into the house all the while that it is shut up shall be unclean until the even.
\v 47 And he that lies in the house shall wash his clothes; and he that eats in the house shall wash his clothes.
\v 48 And if the priest shall come in, and look \add on it\add*, and, behold, the plague has not spread in the house, after the house was plastered: then the priest shall pronounce the house clean, because the plague is healed.
\v 49 And he shall take to cleanse the house two birds, and cedar wood, and scarlet, and hyssop:
\v 50 And he shall kill the one of the birds in an earthen vessel over running water:
\v 51 And he shall take the cedar wood, and the hyssop, and the scarlet, and the living bird, and dip them in the blood of the slain bird, and in the running water, and sprinkle the house seven times:
\v 52 And he shall cleanse the house with the blood of the bird, and with the running water, and with the living bird, and with the cedar wood, and with the hyssop, and with the scarlet:
\v 53 But he shall let go the living bird out of the city into the open fields, and make an atonement for the house: and it shall be clean.
\v 54 This \add is\add* the law for all manner of plague of leprosy, and scale,
\v 55 And for the leprosy of a garment, and of a house,
\v 56 And for a rising, and for a scab, and for a bright spot:
\v 57 To teach when \add it is\add* unclean, and when \add it is\add* clean: this \add is\add* the law of leprosy.
\c 15
\p \v 1 And the LORD spoke to Moses and to Aaron, saying,
\v 2 Speak to the children of Israel, and say to them, When any man has a running issue out of his flesh, \add because of\add* his issue he \add is\add* unclean.
\v 3 And this shall be his uncleanness in his issue: whether his flesh run with his issue, or his flesh be stopped from his issue, it \add is\add* his uncleanness.
\v 4 Every bed, where on he lies that has the issue, is unclean: and every thing, where on he sits, shall be unclean.
\v 5 And whoever touches his bed shall wash his clothes, and bathe \add himself\add* in water, and be unclean until the even.
\v 6 And he that sits on \add any\add* thing where on he sat that has the issue shall wash his clothes, and bathe \add himself\add* in water, and be unclean until the even.
\v 7 And he that touches the flesh of him that has the issue shall wash his clothes, and bathe \add himself\add* in water, and be unclean until the even.
\v 8 And if he that has the issue spit on him that is clean; then he shall wash his clothes, and bathe \add himself\add* in water, and be unclean until the even.
\v 9 And what saddle soever he rides on that has the issue shall be unclean.
\v 10 And whoever touches any thing that was under him shall be unclean until the even: and he that bears \add any of\add* those things shall wash his clothes, and bathe \add himself\add* in water, and be unclean until the even.
\v 11 And whomsoever he touches that has the issue, and has not rinsed his hands in water, he shall wash his clothes, and bathe \add himself\add* in water, and be unclean until the even.
\v 12 And the vessel of earth, that he touches which has the issue, shall be broken: and every vessel of wood shall be rinsed in water.
\v 13 And when he that has an issue is cleansed of his issue; then he shall number to himself seven days for his cleansing, and wash his clothes, and bathe his flesh in running water, and shall be clean.
\v 14 And on the eighth day he shall take to him two turtledoves, or two young pigeons, and come before the LORD to the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, and give them to the priest:
\v 15 And the priest shall offer them, the one \add for\add* a sin offering, and the other \add for\add* a burnt offering; and the priest shall make an atonement for him before the LORD for his issue.
\v 16 And if any man's seed of copulation go out from him, then he shall wash all his flesh in water, and be unclean until the even.
\v 17 And every garment, and every skin, where on is the seed of copulation, shall be washed with water, and be unclean until the even.
\v 18 The woman also with whom man shall lie \add with\add* seed of copulation, they shall \add both\add* bathe \add themselves\add* in water, and be unclean until the even.
\v 19 And if a woman have an issue, \add and\add* her issue in her flesh be blood, she shall be put apart seven days: and whoever touches her shall be unclean until the even.
\v 20 And every thing that she lies on in her separation shall be unclean: every thing also that she sits on shall be unclean.
\v 21 And whoever touches her bed shall wash his clothes, and bathe \add himself\add* in water, and be unclean until the even.
\v 22 And whoever touches any thing that she sat on shall wash his clothes, and bathe \add himself\add* in water, and be unclean until the even.
\v 23 And if it \add be\add* on \add her\add* bed, or on any thing where on she sits, when he touches it, he shall be unclean until the even.
\v 24 And if any man lie with her at all, and her flowers be on him, he shall be unclean seven days; and all the bed where on he lies shall be unclean.
\v 25 And if a woman have an issue of her blood many days out of the time of her separation, or if it run beyond the time of her separation; all the days of the issue of her uncleanness shall be as the days of her separation: she \add shall be\add* unclean.
\v 26 Every bed where on she lies all the days of her issue shall be to her as the bed of her separation: and whatever she sits on shall be unclean, as the uncleanness of her separation.
\v 27 And whoever touches those things shall be unclean, and shall wash his clothes, and bathe \add himself\add* in water, and be unclean until the even.
\v 28 But if she be cleansed of her issue, then she shall number to herself seven days, and after that she shall be clean.
\v 29 And on the eighth day she shall take to her two turtles, or two young pigeons, and bring them to the priest, to the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.
\v 30 And the priest shall offer the one \add for\add* a sin offering, and the other \add for\add* a burnt offering; and the priest shall make an atonement for her before the LORD for the issue of her uncleanness.
\v 31 Thus shall you separate the children of Israel from their uncleanness; that they die not in their uncleanness, when they defile my tabernacle that \add is\add* among them.
\v 32 This \add is\add* the law of him that has an issue, and \add of him\add* whose seed goes from him, and is defiled therewith;
\v 33 And of her that is sick of her flowers, and of him that has an issue, of the man, and of the woman, and of him that lies with her that is unclean.
\c 16
\p \v 1 And the LORD spoke to Moses after the death of the two sons of Aaron, when they offered before the LORD, and died;
\v 2 And the LORD said to Moses, Speak to Aaron your brother, that he come not at all times into the holy \add place\add* within the veil before the mercy seat, which \add is\add* on the ark; that he die not: for I will appear in the cloud on the mercy seat.
\v 3 Thus shall Aaron come into the holy \add place\add*: with a young bullock for a sin offering, and a ram for a burnt offering.
\v 4 He shall put on the holy linen coat, and he shall have the linen breeches on his flesh, and shall be girded with a linen girdle, and with the linen turban shall he be attired: these \add are\add* holy garments; therefore shall he wash his flesh in water, and \add so\add* put them on.
\v 5 And he shall take of the congregation of the children of Israel two kids of the goats for a sin offering, and one ram for a burnt offering.
\v 6 And Aaron shall offer his bullock of the sin offering, which \add is\add* for himself, and make an atonement for himself, and for his house.
\v 7 And he shall take the two goats, and present them before the LORD \add at\add* the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.
\v 8 And Aaron shall cast lots on the two goats; one lot for the LORD, and the other lot for the scapegoat.
\v 9 And Aaron shall bring the goat on which the LORD's lot fell, and offer him \add for\add* a sin offering.
\v 10 But the goat, on which the lot fell to be the scapegoat, shall be presented alive before the LORD, to make an atonement with him, \add and\add* to let him go for a scapegoat into the wilderness.
\v 11 And Aaron shall bring the bullock of the sin offering, which \add is\add* for himself, and shall make an atonement for himself, and for his house, and shall kill the bullock of the sin offering which \add is\add* for himself:
\v 12 And he shall take a censer full of burning coals of fire from off the altar before the LORD, and his hands full of sweet incense beaten small, and bring \add it\add* within the veil:
\v 13 And he shall put the incense on the fire before the LORD, that the cloud of the incense may cover the mercy seat that \add is\add* on the testimony, that he die not:
\v 14 And he shall take of the blood of the bullock, and sprinkle \add it\add* with his finger on the mercy seat eastward; and before the mercy seat shall he sprinkle of the blood with his finger seven times.
\v 15 Then shall he kill the goat of the sin offering, that \add is\add* for the people, and bring his blood within the veil, and do with that blood as he did with the blood of the bullock, and sprinkle it on the mercy seat, and before the mercy seat:
\v 16 And he shall make an atonement for the holy \add place\add*, because of the uncleanness of the children of Israel, and because of their transgressions in all their sins: and so shall he do for the tabernacle of the congregation, that remains among them in the middle of their uncleanness.
\v 17 And there shall be no man in the tabernacle of the congregation when he goes in to make an atonement in the holy \add place\add*, until he come out, and have made an atonement for himself, and for his household, and for all the congregation of Israel.
\v 18 And he shall go out to the altar that \add is\add* before the LORD, and make an atonement for it; and shall take of the blood of the bullock, and of the blood of the goat, and put \add it\add* on the horns of the altar round about.
\v 19 And he shall sprinkle of the blood on it with his finger seven times, and cleanse it, and hallow it from the uncleanness of the children of Israel.
\v 20 And when he has made an end of reconciling the holy \add place\add*, and the tabernacle of the congregation, and the altar, he shall bring the live goat:
\v 21 And Aaron shall lay both his hands on the head of the live goat, and confess over him all the iniquities of the children of Israel, and all their transgressions in all their sins, putting them on the head of the goat, and shall send \add him\add* away by the hand of a fit man into the wilderness:
\v 22 And the goat shall bear on him all their iniquities to a land not inhabited: and he shall let go the goat in the wilderness.
\v 23 And Aaron shall come into the tabernacle of the congregation, and shall put off the linen garments, which he put on when he went into the holy \add place\add*, and shall leave them there:
\v 24 And he shall wash his flesh with water in the holy place, and put on his garments, and come forth, and offer his burnt offering, and the burnt offering of the people, and make an atonement for himself, and for the people.
\v 25 And the fat of the sin offering shall he burn on the altar.
\v 26 And he that let go the goat for the scapegoat shall wash his clothes, and bathe his flesh in water, and afterward come into the camp.
\v 27 And the bullock \add for\add* the sin offering, and the goat \add for\add* the sin offering, whose blood was brought in to make atonement in the holy \add place\add*, shall \add one\add* carry forth without the camp; and they shall burn in the fire their skins, and their flesh, and their dung.
\v 28 And he that burns them shall wash his clothes, and bathe his flesh in water, and afterward he shall come into the camp.
\v 29 And \add this\add* shall be a statute for ever to you: \add that\add* in the seventh month, on the tenth \add day\add* of the month, you shall afflict your souls, and do no work at all, \add whether it be\add* one of your own country, or a stranger that sojournes among you:
\v 30 For on that day shall \add the priest\add* make an atonement for you, to cleanse you, \add that\add* you may be clean from all your sins before the LORD.
\v 31 It \add shall be\add* a sabbath of rest to you, and you shall afflict your souls, by a statute for ever.
\v 32 And the priest, whom he shall anoint, and whom he shall consecrate to minister in the priest's office in his father's stead, shall make the atonement, and shall put on the linen clothes, \add even\add* the holy garments:
\v 33 And he shall make an atonement for the holy sanctuary, and he shall make an atonement for the tabernacle of the congregation, and for the altar, and he shall make an atonement for the priests, and for all the people of the congregation.
\v 34 And this shall be an everlasting statute to you, to make an atonement for the children of Israel for all their sins once a year. And he did as the LORD commanded Moses.
\c 17
\p \v 1 And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
\v 2 Speak to Aaron, and to his sons, and to all the children of Israel, and say to them; This \add is\add* the thing which the LORD has commanded, saying,
\v 3 What man soever \add there be\add* of the house of Israel, that kills an ox, or lamb, or goat, in the camp, or that kills \add it\add* out of the camp,
\v 4 And brings it not to the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, to offer an offering to the LORD before the tabernacle of the LORD; blood shall be imputed to that man; he has shed blood; and that man shall be cut off from among his people:
\v 5 To the end that the children of Israel may bring their sacrifices, which they offer in the open field, even that they may bring them to the LORD, to the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, to the priest, and offer them \add for\add* peace offerings to the LORD.
\v 6 And the priest shall sprinkle the blood on the altar of the LORD \add at\add* the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, and burn the fat for a sweet smell to the LORD.
\v 7 And they shall no more offer their sacrifices to devils, after whom they have gone a whoring. This shall be a statute for ever to them throughout their generations.
\v 8 And you shall say to them, Whatever man \add there be\add* of the house of Israel, or of the strangers which sojourn among you, that offers a burnt offering or sacrifice,
\v 9 And brings it not to the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, to offer it to the LORD; even that man shall be cut off from among his people.
\v 10 And whatever man \add there be\add* of the house of Israel, or of the strangers that sojourn among you, that eats any manner of blood; I will even set my face against that soul that eats blood, and will cut him off from among his people.
\v 11 For the life of the flesh \add is\add* in the blood: and I have given it to you on the altar to make an atonement for your souls: for it \add is\add* the blood \add that\add* makes an atonement for the soul.
\v 12 Therefore I said to the children of Israel, No soul of you shall eat blood, neither shall any stranger that sojournes among you eat blood.
\v 13 And whatever man \add there be\add* of the children of Israel, or of the strangers that sojourn among you, which hunts and catches any beast or fowl that may be eaten; he shall even pour out the blood thereof, and cover it with dust.
\v 14 For \add it is\add* the life of all flesh; the blood of it \add is\add* for the life thereof: therefore I said to the children of Israel, You shall eat the blood of no manner of flesh: for the life of all flesh \add is\add* the blood thereof: whoever eats it shall be cut off.
\v 15 And every soul that eats that which died \add of itself\add*, or that which was torn \add with beasts\add*, \add whether it be\add* one of your own country, or a stranger, he shall both wash his clothes, and bathe \add himself\add* in water, and be unclean until the even: then shall he be clean.
\v 16 But if he wash \add them\add* not, nor bathe his flesh; then he shall bear his iniquity.
\c 18
\p \v 1 And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
\v 2 Speak to the children of Israel, and say to them, I am the LORD your God.
\v 3 After the doings of the land of Egypt, wherein you dwelled, shall you not do: and after the doings of the land of Canaan, where I bring you, shall you not do: neither shall you walk in their ordinances.
\v 4 You shall do my judgments, and keep my ordinances, to walk therein: I \add am\add* the LORD your God.
\v 5 You shall therefore keep my statutes, and my judgments: which if a man do, he shall live in them: I \add am\add* the LORD.
\v 6 None of you shall approach to any that is near of kin to him, to uncover \add their\add* nakedness: I \add am\add* the LORD.
\v 7 The nakedness of your father, or the nakedness of your mother, shall you not uncover: she \add is\add* your mother; you shall not uncover her nakedness.
\v 8 The nakedness of your father's wife shall you not uncover: it \add is\add* your father's nakedness.
\v 9 The nakedness of your sister, the daughter of your father, or daughter of your mother, \add whether she be\add* born at home, or born abroad, \add even\add* their nakedness you shall not uncover.
\v 10 The nakedness of your son's daughter, or of your daughter's daughter, \add even\add* their nakedness you shall not uncover: for theirs \add is\add* your own nakedness.
\v 11 The nakedness of your father's wife's daughter, begotten of your father, she \add is\add* your sister, you shall not uncover her nakedness.
\v 12 You shall not uncover the nakedness of your father's sister: she \add is\add* your father's near kinswoman.
\v 13 You shall not uncover the nakedness of your mother's sister: for she \add is\add* your mother's near kinswoman.
\v 14 You shall not uncover the nakedness of your father's brother, you shall not approach to his wife: she \add is\add* your aunt.
\v 15 You shall not uncover the nakedness of your daughter in law: she \add is\add* your son's wife; you shall not uncover her nakedness.
\v 16 You shall not uncover the nakedness of your brother's wife: it \add is\add* your brother's nakedness.
\v 17 You shall not uncover the nakedness of a woman and her daughter, neither shall you take her son's daughter, or her daughter's daughter, to uncover her nakedness; \add for\add* they \add are\add* her near kinswomen: it \add is\add* wickedness.
\v 18 Neither shall you take a wife to her sister, to vex \add her\add*, to uncover her nakedness, beside the other in her life \add time\add*.
\v 19 Also you shall not approach to a woman to uncover her nakedness, as long as she is put apart for her uncleanness.
\v 20 Moreover you shall not lie carnally with your neighbor's wife, to defile yourself with her.
\v 21 And you shall not let any of your seed pass through \add the fire\add* to Molech, neither shall you profane the name of your God: I \add am\add* the LORD.
\v 22 You shall not lie with mankind, as with womankind: it \add is\add* abomination.
\v 23 Neither shall you lie with any beast to defile yourself therewith: neither shall any woman stand before a beast to lie down thereto: it \add is\add* confusion.
\v 24 Defile not you yourselves in any of these things: for in all these the nations are defiled which I cast out before you:
\v 25 And the land is defiled: therefore I do visit the iniquity thereof on it, and the land itself vomits out her inhabitants.
\v 26 You shall therefore keep my statutes and my judgments, and shall not commit \add any\add* of these abominations; \add neither\add* any of your own nation, nor any stranger that sojournes among you:
\v 27 (For all these abominations have the men of the land done, which \add were\add* before you, and the land is defiled;)
\v 28 That the land spew not you out also, when you defile it, as it spewed out the nations that \add were\add* before you.
\v 29 For whoever shall commit any of these abominations, even the souls that commit \add them\add* shall be cut off from among their people.
\v 30 Therefore shall you keep my ordinance, that \add you\add* commit not \add any one\add* of these abominable customs, which were committed before you, and that you defile not yourselves therein: I \add am\add* the LORD your God.
\c 19
\p \v 1 And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
\v 2 Speak to all the congregation of the children of Israel, and say to them, You shall be holy: for I the LORD your God \add am\add* holy.
\v 3 You shall fear every man his mother, and his father, and keep my sabbaths: I \add am\add* the LORD your God.
\v 4 Turn you not to idols, nor make to yourselves molten gods: I \add am\add* the LORD your God.
\v 5 And if you offer a sacrifice of peace offerings to the LORD, you shall offer it at your own will.
\v 6 It shall be eaten the same day you offer it, and on the morrow: and if ought remain until the third day, it shall be burnt in the fire.
\v 7 And if it be eaten at all on the third day, it \add is\add* abominable; it shall not be accepted.
\v 8 Therefore \add every one\add* that eats it shall bear his iniquity, because he has profaned the hallowed thing of the LORD: and that soul shall be cut off from among his people.
\v 9 And when you reap the harvest of your land, you shall not wholly reap the corners of your field, neither shall you gather the gleanings of your harvest.
\v 10 And you shall not glean your vineyard, neither shall you gather \add every\add* grape of your vineyard; you shall leave them for the poor and stranger: I \add am\add* the LORD your God.
\v 11 You shall not steal, neither deal falsely, neither lie one to another.
\v 12 And you shall not swear by my name falsely, neither shall you profane the name of your God: I \add am\add* the LORD.
\v 13 You shall not defraud your neighbor, neither rob \add him\add*: the wages of him that is hired shall not abide with you all night until the morning.
\v 14 You shall not curse the deaf, nor put a stumbling block before the blind, but shall fear your God: I \add am\add* the LORD.
\v 15 You shall do no unrighteousness in judgment: you shall not respect the person of the poor, nor honor the person of the mighty: \add but\add* in righteousness shall you judge your neighbor.
\v 16 You shall not go up and down \add as\add* a talebearer among your people: neither shall you stand against the blood of your neighbor; I \add am\add* the LORD.
\v 17 You shall not hate your brother in your heart: you shall in any wise rebuke your neighbor, and not suffer sin on him.
\v 18 You shall not avenge, nor bear any grudge against the children of your people, but you shall love your neighbor as yourself: I \add am\add* the LORD.
\v 19 You shall keep my statutes. You shall not let your cattle engender with a diverse kind: you shall not sow your field with mingled seed: neither shall a garment mingled of linen and woolen come on you.
\v 20 And whoever lies carnally with a woman, that \add is\add* a female slave, betrothed to an husband, and not at all redeemed, nor freedom given her; she shall be scourged; they shall not be put to death, because she was not free.
\v 21 And he shall bring his trespass offering to the LORD, to the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, \add even\add* a ram for a trespass offering.
\v 22 And the priest shall make an atonement for him with the ram of the trespass offering before the LORD for his sin which he has done: and the sin which he has done shall be forgiven him.
\v 23 And when you shall come into the land, and shall have planted all manner of trees for food, then you shall count the fruit thereof as uncircumcised: three years shall it be as uncircumcised to you: it shall not be eaten of.
\v 24 But in the fourth year all the fruit thereof shall be holy to praise the LORD \add with\add*.
\v 25 And in the fifth year shall you eat of the fruit thereof, that it may yield to you the increase thereof: I \add am\add* the LORD your God.
\v 26 You shall not eat \add any thing\add* with the blood: neither shall you use enchantment, nor observe times.
\v 27 You shall not round the corners of your heads, neither shall you mar the corners of your beard.
\v 28 You shall not make any cuttings in your flesh for the dead, nor print any marks on you: I \add am\add* the LORD.
\v 29 Do not prostitute your daughter, to cause her to be a whore; lest the land fall to prostitution, and the land become full of wickedness.
\v 30 You shall keep my sabbaths, and reverence my sanctuary: I \add am\add* the LORD.
\v 31 Regard not them that have familiar spirits, neither seek after wizards, to be defiled by them: I \add am\add* the LORD your God.
\v 32 You shall rise up before the hoary head, and honor the face of the old man, and fear your God: I \add am\add* the LORD.
\v 33 And if a stranger sojourn with you in your land, you shall not vex him.
\v 34 \add But\add* the stranger that dwells with you shall be to you as one born among you, and you shall love him as yourself; for you were strangers in the land of Egypt: I \add am\add* the LORD your God.
\v 35 You shall do no unrighteousness in judgment, in length, in weight, or in measure.
\v 36 Just balances, just weights, a just ephah, and a just hin, shall you have: I \add am\add* the LORD your God, which brought you out of the land of Egypt.
\v 37 Therefore shall you observe all my statutes, and all my judgments, and do them: I \add am\add* the LORD.
\c 20
\p \v 1 And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
\v 2 Again, you shall say to the children of Israel, Whoever \add he be\add* of the children of Israel, or of the strangers that sojourn in Israel, that gives \add any\add* of his seed to Molech; he shall surely be put to death: the people of the land shall stone him with stones.
\v 3 And I will set my face against that man, and will cut him off from among his people; because he has given of his seed to Molech, to defile my sanctuary, and to profane my holy name.
\v 4 And if the people of the land do any ways hide their eyes from the man, when he gives of his seed to Molech, and kill him not:
\v 5 Then I will set my face against that man, and against his family, and will cut him off, and all that go a whoring after him, to commit prostitution with Molech, from among their people.
\v 6 And the soul that turns after such as have familiar spirits, and after wizards, to go a whoring after them, I will even set my face against that soul, and will cut him off from among his people.
\v 7 Sanctify yourselves therefore, and be you holy: for I \add am\add* the LORD your God.
\v 8 And you shall keep my statutes, and do them: I \add am\add* the LORD which sanctify you.
\v 9 For every one that curses his father or his mother shall be surely put to death: he has cursed his father or his mother; his blood \add shall be\add* on him.
\v 10 And the man that commits adultery with \add another\add* man's wife, \add even he\add* that commits adultery with his neighbor's wife, the adulterer and the adulteress shall surely be put to death.
\v 11 And the man that lies with his father's wife has uncovered his father's nakedness: both of them shall surely be put to death; their blood \add shall be\add* on them.
\v 12 And if a man lie with his daughter in law, both of them shall surely be put to death: they have worked confusion; their blood \add shall be\add* on them.
\v 13 If a man also lie with mankind, as he lies with a woman, both of them have committed an abomination: they shall surely be put to death; their blood \add shall be\add* on them.
\v 14 And if a man take a wife and her mother, it \add is\add* wickedness: they shall be burnt with fire, both he and they; that there be no wickedness among you.
\v 15 And if a man lie with a beast, he shall surely be put to death: and you shall slay the beast.
\v 16 And if a woman approach to any beast, and lie down thereto, you shall kill the woman, and the beast: they shall surely be put to death; their blood \add shall be\add* on them.
\v 17 And if a man shall take his sister, his father's daughter, or his mother's daughter, and see her nakedness, and she see his nakedness; it \add is\add* a wicked thing; and they shall be cut off in the sight of their people: he has uncovered his sister's nakedness; he shall bear his iniquity.
\v 18 And if a man shall lie with a woman having her sickness, and shall uncover her nakedness; he has discovered her fountain, and she has uncovered the fountain of her blood: and both of them shall be cut off from among their people.
\v 19 And you shall not uncover the nakedness of your mother's sister, nor of your father's sister: for he uncovers his near kin: they shall bear their iniquity.
\v 20 And if a man shall lie with his uncle's wife, he has uncovered his uncle's nakedness: they shall bear their sin; they shall die childless.
\v 21 And if a man shall take his brother's wife, it \add is\add* an unclean thing: he has uncovered his brother's nakedness; they shall be childless.
\v 22 You shall therefore keep all my statutes, and all my judgments, and do them: that the land, where I bring you to dwell therein, spew you not out.
\v 23 And you shall not walk in the manners of the nation, which I cast out before you: for they committed all these things, and therefore I abhorred them.
\v 24 But I have said to you, You shall inherit their land, and I will give it to you to possess it, a land that flows with milk and honey: I \add am\add* the LORD your God, which have separated you from \add other\add* people.
\v 25 You shall therefore put difference between clean beasts and unclean, and between unclean fowls and clean: and you shall not make your souls abominable by beast, or by fowl, or by any manner of living thing that creeps on the ground, which I have separated from you as unclean.
\v 26 And you shall be holy to me: for I the LORD \add am\add* holy, and have severed you from \add other\add* people, that you should be mine.
\v 27 A man also or woman that has a familiar spirit, or that is a wizard, shall surely be put to death: they shall stone them with stones: their blood \add shall be\add* on them.
\c 21
\p \v 1 And the LORD said to Moses, Speak to the priests the sons of Aaron, and say to them, There shall none be defiled for the dead among his people:
\v 2 But for his kin, that is near to him, \add that is\add*, for his mother, and for his father, and for his son, and for his daughter, and for his brother.
\v 3 And for his sister a virgin, that is near to him, which has had no husband; for her may he be defiled.
\v 4 \add But\add* he shall not defile himself, \add being\add* a chief man among his people, to profane himself.
\v 5 They shall not make baldness on their head, neither shall they shave off the corner of their beard, nor make any cuttings in their flesh.
\v 6 They shall be holy to their God, and not profane the name of their God: for the offerings of the LORD made by fire, \add and\add* the bread of their God, they do offer: therefore they shall be holy.
\v 7 They shall not take a wife \add that is\add* a whore, or profane; neither shall they take a woman put away from her husband: for he \add is\add* holy to his God.
\v 8 You shall sanctify him therefore; for he offers the bread of your God: he shall be holy to you: for I the LORD, which sanctify you, \add am\add* holy.
\v 9 And the daughter of any priest, if she profane herself by playing the whore, she profanes her father: she shall be burnt with fire.
\v 10 And \add he that is\add* the high priest among his brothers, on whose head the anointing oil was poured, and that is consecrated to put on the garments, shall not uncover his head, nor rend his clothes;
\v 11 Neither shall he go in to any dead body, nor defile himself for his father, or for his mother;
\v 12 Neither shall he go out of the sanctuary, nor profane the sanctuary of his God; for the crown of the anointing oil of his God \add is\add* on him: I \add am\add* the LORD.
\v 13 And he shall take a wife in her virginity.
\v 14 A widow, or a divorced woman, or profane, \add or\add* an harlot, these shall he not take: but he shall take a virgin of his own people to wife.
\v 15 Neither shall he profane his seed among his people: for I the LORD do sanctify him.
\v 16 And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
\v 17 Speak to Aaron, saying, Whoever \add he be\add* of your seed in their generations that has \add any\add* blemish, let him not approach to offer the bread of his God.
\v 18 For whatever man \add he be\add* that has a blemish, he shall not approach: a blind man, or a lame, or he that has a flat nose, or any thing superfluous,
\v 19 Or a man that is broken footed, or broken handed,
\v 20 Or hunch back, or a dwarf, or that has a blemish in his eye, or be scurvy, or scabbed, or has his stones broken;
\v 21 No man that has a blemish of the seed of Aaron the priest shall come near to offer the offerings of the LORD made by fire: he has a blemish; he shall not come near to offer the bread of his God.
\v 22 He shall eat the bread of his God, \add both\add* of the most holy, and of the holy.
\v 23 Only he shall not go in to the veil, nor come near to the altar, because he has a blemish; that he profane not my sanctuaries: for I the LORD do sanctify them.
\v 24 And Moses told \add it\add* to Aaron, and to his sons, and to all the children of Israel.
\c 22
\p \v 1 And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
\v 2 Speak to Aaron and to his sons, that they separate themselves from the holy things of the children of Israel, and that they profane not my holy name \add in those things\add* which they hallow to me: I \add am\add* the LORD.
\v 3 Say to them, Whoever \add he be\add* of all your seed among your generations, that goes to the holy things, which the children of Israel hallow to the LORD, having his uncleanness on him, that soul shall be cut off from my presence: I \add am\add* the LORD.
\v 4 What man soever of the seed of Aaron \add is\add* a leper, or has a running issue; he shall not eat of the holy things, until he be clean. And whoever touches any thing \add that is\add* unclean \add by\add* the dead, or a man whose seed goes from him;
\v 5 Or whoever touches any creeping thing, whereby he may be made unclean, or a man of whom he may take uncleanness, whatever uncleanness he has;
\v 6 The soul which has touched any such shall be unclean until even, and shall not eat of the holy things, unless he wash his flesh with water.
\v 7 And when the sun is down, he shall be clean, and shall afterward eat of the holy things; because it \add is\add* his food.
\v 8 That which dies of itself, or is torn \add with beasts\add*, he shall not eat to defile himself therewith; I \add am\add* the LORD.
\v 9 They shall therefore keep my ordinance, lest they bear sin for it, and die therefore, if they profane it: I the LORD do sanctify them.
\v 10 There shall no stranger eat \add of\add* the holy thing: a sojourner of the priest, or an hired servant, shall not eat \add of\add* the holy thing.
\v 11 But if the priest buy \add any\add* soul with his money, he shall eat of it, and he that is born in his house: they shall eat of his meat.
\v 12 If the priest's daughter also be \add married\add* to a stranger, she may not eat of an offering of the holy things.
\v 13 But if the priest's daughter be a widow, or divorced, and have no child, and is returned to her father's house, as in her youth, she shall eat of her father's meat: but there shall be no stranger eat thereof.
\v 14 And if a man eat \add of\add* the holy thing unwittingly, then he shall put the fifth \add part\add* thereof to it, and shall give \add it\add* to the priest with the holy thing.
\v 15 And they shall not profane the holy things of the children of Israel, which they offer to the LORD;
\v 16 Or suffer them to bear the iniquity of trespass, when they eat their holy things: for I the LORD do sanctify them.
\v 17 And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
\v 18 Speak to Aaron, and to his sons, and to all the children of Israel, and say to them, Whatever \add he be\add* of the house of Israel, or of the strangers in Israel, that will offer his oblation for all his vows, and for all his freewill offerings, which they will offer to the LORD for a burnt offering;
\v 19 \add You shall offer\add* at your own will a male without blemish, of the beeves, of the sheep, or of the goats.
\v 20 \add But\add* whatever has a blemish, \add that\add* shall you not offer: for it shall not be acceptable for you.
\v 21 And whoever offers a sacrifice of peace offerings to the LORD to accomplish \add his\add* vow, or a freewill offering in beeves or sheep, it shall be perfect to be accepted; there shall be no blemish therein.
\v 22 Blind, or broken, or maimed, or having a running sore, or scurvy, or scabbed, you shall not offer these to the LORD, nor make an offering by fire of them on the altar to the LORD.
\v 23 Either a bullock or a lamb that has any thing superfluous or lacking in his parts, that may you offer \add for\add* a freewill offering; but for a vow it shall not be accepted.
\v 24 You shall not offer to the LORD that which is bruised, or crushed, or broken, or cut; neither shall you make \add any offering thereof\add* in your land.
\v 25 Neither from a stranger's hand shall you offer the bread of your God of any of these; because their corruption \add is\add* in them, \add and\add* blemishes \add be\add* in them: they shall not be accepted for you.
\v 26 And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
\v 27 When a bullock, or a sheep, or a goat, is brought forth, then it shall be seven days under the dam; and from the eighth day and thereafter it shall be accepted for an offering made by fire to the LORD.
\v 28 And \add whether it be\add* cow, or ewe, you shall not kill it and her young both in one day.
\v 29 And when you will offer a sacrifice of thanksgiving to the LORD, offer \add it\add* at your own will.
\v 30 On the same day it shall be eaten up; you shall leave none of it until the morrow: I \add am\add* the LORD.
\v 31 Therefore shall you keep my commandments, and do them: I \add am\add* the LORD.
\v 32 Neither shall you profane my holy name; but I will be hallowed among the children of Israel: I \add am\add* the LORD which hallow you,
\v 33 That brought you out of the land of Egypt, to be your God: I \add am\add* the LORD.
\c 23
\p \v 1 And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
\v 2 Speak to the children of Israel, and say to them, \add Concerning\add* the feasts of the LORD, which you shall proclaim \add to be\add* holy convocations, \add even\add* these \add are\add* my feasts.
\v 3 Six days shall work be done: but the seventh day \add is\add* the sabbath of rest, an holy convocation; you shall do no work \add therein\add*: it \add is\add* the sabbath of the LORD in all your dwellings.
\v 4 These \add are\add* the feasts of the LORD, \add even\add* holy convocations, which you shall proclaim in their seasons.
\v 5 In the fourteenth \add day\add* of the first month at even \add is\add* the LORD's passover.
\v 6 And on the fifteenth day of the same month \add is\add* the feast of unleavened bread to the LORD: seven days you must eat unleavened bread.
\v 7 In the first day you shall have an holy convocation: you shall do no servile work therein.
\v 8 But you shall offer an offering made by fire to the LORD seven days: in the seventh day \add is\add* an holy convocation: you shall do no servile work \add therein\add*.
\v 9 And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
\v 10 Speak to the children of Israel, and say to them, When you be come into the land which I give to you, and shall reap the harvest thereof, then you shall bring a sheaf of the first fruits of your harvest to the priest:
\v 11 And he shall wave the sheaf before the LORD, to be accepted for you: on the morrow after the sabbath the priest shall wave it.
\v 12 And you shall offer that day when you wave the sheaf an he lamb without blemish of the first year for a burnt offering to the LORD.
\v 13 And the meat offering thereof \add shall be\add* two tenth deals of fine flour mingled with oil, an offering made by fire to the LORD \add for\add* a sweet smell: and the drink offering thereof \add shall be\add* of wine, the fourth \add part\add* of an hin.
\v 14 And you shall eat neither bread, nor parched corn, nor green ears, until the selfsame day that you have brought an offering to your God: \add it shall be\add* a statute for ever throughout your generations in all your dwellings.
\v 15 And you shall count to you from the morrow after the sabbath, from the day that you brought the sheaf of the wave offering; seven sabbaths shall be complete:
\v 16 Even to the morrow after the seventh sabbath shall you number fifty days; and you shall offer a new meat offering to the LORD.
\v 17 You shall bring out of your habitations two wave loaves of two tenth deals; they shall be of fine flour; they shall be baked with leaven; \add they are\add* the first fruits to the LORD.
\v 18 And you shall offer with the bread seven lambs without blemish of the first year, and one young bullock, and two rams: they shall be \add for\add* a burnt offering to the LORD, with their meat offering, and their drink offerings, \add even\add* an offering made by fire, of sweet smell to the LORD.
\v 19 Then you shall sacrifice one kid of the goats for a sin offering, and two lambs of the first year for a sacrifice of peace offerings.
\v 20 And the priest shall wave them with the bread of the first fruits \add for\add* a wave offering before the LORD, with the two lambs: they shall be holy to the LORD for the priest.
\v 21 And you shall proclaim on the selfsame day, \add that\add* it may be an holy convocation to you: you shall do no servile work \add therein\add*: \add it shall be\add* a statute for ever in all your dwellings throughout your generations.
\v 22 And when you reap the harvest of your land, you shall not make clean riddance of the corners of your field when you reap, neither shall you gather any gleaning of your harvest: you shall leave them to the poor, and to the stranger: I \add am\add* the LORD your God.
\v 23 And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
\v 24 Speak to the children of Israel, saying, In the seventh month, in the first \add day\add* of the month, shall you have a sabbath, a memorial of blowing of trumpets, an holy convocation.
\v 25 You shall do no servile work \add therein\add*: but you shall offer an offering made by fire to the LORD.
\v 26 And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
\v 27 Also on the tenth \add day\add* of this seventh month \add there shall be\add* a day of atonement: it shall be an holy convocation to you; and you shall afflict your souls, and offer an offering made by fire to the LORD.
\v 28 And you shall do no work in that same day: for it \add is\add* a day of atonement, to make an atonement for you before the LORD your God.
\v 29 For whatever soul \add it be\add* that shall not be afflicted in that same day, he shall be cut off from among his people.
\v 30 And whatever soul \add it be\add* that does any work in that same day, the same soul will I destroy from among his people.
\v 31 You shall do no manner of work: \add it shall be\add* a statute for ever throughout your generations in all your dwellings.
\v 32 It \add shall be\add* to you a sabbath of rest, and you shall afflict your souls: in the ninth \add day\add* of the month at even, from even to even, shall you celebrate your sabbath.
\v 33 And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
\v 34 Speak to the children of Israel, saying, The fifteenth day of this seventh month \add shall be\add* the feast of tabernacles \add for\add* seven days to the LORD.
\v 35 On the first day \add shall be\add* an holy convocation: you shall do no servile work \add therein\add*.
\v 36 Seven days you shall offer an offering made by fire to the LORD: on the eighth day shall be an holy convocation to you; and you shall offer an offering made by fire to the LORD: it \add is\add* a solemn assembly; \add and\add* you shall do no servile work \add therein\add*.
\v 37 These \add are\add* the feasts of the LORD, which you shall proclaim \add to be\add* holy convocations, to offer an offering made by fire to the LORD, a burnt offering, and a meat offering, a sacrifice, and drink offerings, every thing on his day:
\v 38 Beside the sabbaths of the LORD, and beside your gifts, and beside all your vows, and beside all your freewill offerings, which you give to the LORD.
\v 39 Also in the fifteenth day of the seventh month, when you have gathered in the fruit of the land, you shall keep a feast to the LORD seven days: on the first day \add shall be\add* a sabbath, and on the eighth day \add shall be\add* a sabbath.
\v 40 And you shall take you on the first day the boughs of goodly trees, branches of palm trees, and the boughs of thick trees, and willows of the brook; and you shall rejoice before the LORD your God seven days.
\v 41 And you shall keep it a feast to the LORD seven days in the year. \add It shall be\add* a statute for ever in your generations: you shall celebrate it in the seventh month.
\v 42 You shall dwell in booths seven days; all that are Israelites born shall dwell in booths:
\v 43 That your generations may know that I made the children of Israel to dwell in booths, when I brought them out of the land of Egypt: I \add am\add* the LORD your God.
\v 44 And Moses declared to the children of Israel the feasts of the LORD.
\c 24
\p \v 1 And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
\v 2 Command the children of Israel, that they bring to you pure oil olive beaten for the light, to cause the lamps to burn continually.
\v 3 Without the veil of the testimony, in the tabernacle of the congregation, shall Aaron order it from the evening to the morning before the LORD continually: \add it shall be\add* a statute for ever in your generations.
\v 4 He shall order the lamps on the pure candlestick before the LORD continually.
\v 5 And you shall take fine flour, and bake twelve cakes thereof: two tenth deals shall be in one cake.
\v 6 And you shall set them in two rows, six on a row, on the pure table before the LORD.
\v 7 And you shall put pure frankincense on \add each\add* row, that it may be on the bread for a memorial, \add even\add* an offering made by fire to the LORD.
\v 8 Every sabbath he shall set it in order before the LORD continually, \add being taken\add* from the children of Israel by an everlasting covenant.
\v 9 And it shall be Aaron's and his sons'; and they shall eat it in the holy place: for it \add is\add* most holy to him of the offerings of the LORD made by fire by a perpetual statute.
\v 10 And the son of an Israelitish woman, whose father \add was\add* an Egyptian, went out among the children of Israel: and this son of the Israelitish \add woman\add* and a man of Israel strove together in the camp;
\v 11 And the Israelitish woman's son blasphemed the name \add of the Lord\add*, and cursed. And they brought him to Moses: (and his mother's name \add was\add* Shelomith, the daughter of Dibri, of the tribe of Dan:)
\v 12 And they put him in ward, that the mind of the LORD might be showed them.
\v 13 And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
\v 14 Bring forth him that has cursed without the camp; and let all that heard \add him\add* lay their hands on his head, and let all the congregation stone him.
\v 15 And you shall speak to the children of Israel, saying, Whoever curses his God shall bear his sin.
\v 16 And he that blasphemes the name of the LORD, he shall surely be put to death, \add and\add* all the congregation shall certainly stone him: as well the stranger, as he that is born in the land, when he blasphemes the name \add of the Lord\add*, shall be put to death.
\v 17 And he that kills any man shall surely be put to death.
\v 18 And he that kills a beast shall make it good; beast for beast.
\v 19 And if a man cause a blemish in his neighbor; as he has done, so shall it be done to him;
\v 20 Breach for breach, eye for eye, tooth for tooth: as he has caused a blemish in a man, so shall it be done to him \add again\add*.
\v 21 And he that kills a beast, he shall restore it: and he that kills a man, he shall be put to death.
\v 22 You shall have one manner of law, as well for the stranger, as for one of your own country: for I \add am\add* the LORD your God.
\v 23 And Moses spoke to the children of Israel, that they should bring forth him that had cursed out of the camp, and stone him with stones. And the children of Israel did as the LORD commanded Moses.
\c 25
\p \v 1 And the LORD spoke to Moses in mount Sinai, saying,
\v 2 Speak to the children of Israel, and say to them, When you come into the land which I give you, then shall the land keep a sabbath to the LORD.
\v 3 Six years you shall sow your field, and six years you shall prune your vineyard, and gather in the fruit thereof;
\v 4 But in the seventh year shall be a sabbath of rest to the land, a sabbath for the LORD: you shall neither sow your field, nor prune your vineyard.
\v 5 That which grows of its own accord of your harvest you shall not reap, neither gather the grapes of your vine undressed: \add for\add* it is a year of rest to the land.
\v 6 And the sabbath of the land shall be meat for you; for you, and for your servant, and for your maid, and for your hired servant, and for your stranger that sojournes with you.
\v 7 And for your cattle, and for the beast that \add are\add* in your land, shall all the increase thereof be meat.
\v 8 And you shall number seven sabbaths of years to you, seven times seven years; and the space of the seven sabbaths of years shall be to you forty and nine years.
\v 9 Then shall you cause the trumpet of the jubilee to sound on the tenth \add day\add* of the seventh month, in the day of atonement shall you make the trumpet sound throughout all your land.
\v 10 And you shall hallow the fiftieth year, and proclaim liberty throughout \add all\add* the land to all the inhabitants thereof: it shall be a jubilee to you; and you shall return every man to his possession, and you shall return every man to his family.
\v 11 A jubilee shall that fiftieth year be to you: you shall not sow, neither reap that which grows of itself in it, nor gather \add the grapes\add* in it of your vine undressed.
\v 12 For it \add is\add* the jubilee; it shall be holy to you: you shall eat the increase thereof out of the field.
\v 13 In the year of this jubilee you shall return every man to his possession.
\v 14 And if you sell ought to your neighbor, or buy \add ought\add* of your neighbor's hand, you shall not oppress one another:
\v 15 According to the number of years after the jubilee you shall buy of your neighbor, \add and\add* according to the number of years of the fruits he shall sell to you:
\v 16 According to the multitude of years you shall increase the price thereof, and according to the fewness of years you shall diminish the price of it: for \add according\add* to the number \add of the years\add* of the fruits does he sell to you.
\v 17 You shall not therefore oppress one another; but you shall fear your God: for I \add am\add* the LORD your God.
\v 18 Why you shall do my statutes, and keep my judgments, and do them; and you shall dwell in the land in safety.
\v 19 And the land shall yield her fruit, and you shall eat your fill, and dwell therein in safety.
\v 20 And if you shall say, What shall we eat the seventh year? behold, we shall not sow, nor gather in our increase:
\v 21 Then I will command my blessing on you in the sixth year, and it shall bring forth fruit for three years.
\v 22 And you shall sow the eighth year, and eat \add yet\add* of old fruit until the ninth year; until her fruits come in you shall eat \add of\add* the old \add store\add*.
\v 23 The land shall not be sold for ever: for the land \add is\add* mine, for you \add are\add* strangers and sojourners with me.
\v 24 And in all the land of your possession you shall grant a redemption for the land.
\v 25 If your brother be waxen poor, and has sold away \add some\add* of his possession, and if any of his kin come to redeem it, then shall he redeem that which his brother sold.
\v 26 And if the man have none to redeem it, and himself be able to redeem it;
\v 27 Then let him count the years of the sale thereof, and restore the remainder to the man to whom he sold it; that he may return to his possession.
\v 28 But if he be not able to restore \add it\add* to him, then that which is sold shall remain in the hand of him that has bought it until the year of jubilee: and in the jubilee it shall go out, and he shall return to his possession.
\v 29 And if a man sell a dwelling house in a walled city, then he may redeem it within a whole year after it is sold; \add within\add* a full year may he redeem it.
\v 30 And if it be not redeemed within the space of a full year, then the house that \add is\add* in the walled city shall be established for ever to him that bought it throughout his generations: it shall not go out in the jubilee.
\v 31 But the houses of the villages which have no wall round about them shall be counted as the fields of the country: they may be redeemed, and they shall go out in the jubilee.
\v 32 Notwithstanding the cities of the Levites, \add and\add* the houses of the cities of their possession, may the Levites redeem at any time.
\v 33 And if a man purchase of the Levites, then the house that was sold, and the city of his possession, shall go out in \add the year of\add* jubilee: for the houses of the cities of the Levites \add are\add* their possession among the children of Israel.
\v 34 But the field of the suburbs of their cities may not be sold; for it \add is\add* their perpetual possession.
\v 35 And if your brother be waxen poor, and fallen in decay with you; then you shall relieve him: \add yes\add*, \add though he be\add* a stranger, or a sojourner; that he may live with you.
\v 36 Take you no usury of him, or increase: but fear your God; that your brother may live with you.
\v 37 You shall not give him your money on usury, nor lend him your victuals for increase.
\v 38 I \add am\add* the LORD your God, which brought you forth out of the land of Egypt, to give you the land of Canaan, \add and\add* to be your God.
\v 39 And if your brother \add that dwells\add* by you be waxen poor, and be sold to you; you shall not compel him to serve as a bondservant:
\v 40 \add But\add* as an hired servant, \add and\add* as a sojourner, he shall be with you, \add and\add* shall serve you to the year of jubilee.
\v 41 And \add then\add* shall he depart from you, \add both\add* he and his children with him, and shall return to his own family, and to the possession of his fathers shall he return.
\v 42 For they \add are\add* my servants, which I brought forth out of the land of Egypt: they shall not be sold as slaves.
\v 43 You shall not rule over him with rigor; but shall fear your God.
\v 44 Both your slaves, and your bondmaids, which you shall have, \add shall be\add* of the heathen that are round about you; of them shall you buy slaves and bondmaids.
\v 45 Moreover of the children of the strangers that do sojourn among you, of them shall you buy, and of their families that \add are\add* with you, which they begat in your land: and they shall be your possession.
\v 46 And you shall take them as an inheritance for your children after you, to inherit \add them for\add* a possession; they shall be your slaves for ever: but over your brothers the children of Israel, you shall not rule one over another with rigor.
\v 47 And if a sojourner or stranger wax rich by you, and your brother \add that dwells\add* by him wax poor, and sell himself to the stranger \add or\add* sojourner by you, or to the stock of the stranger's family:
\v 48 After that he is sold he may be redeemed again; one of his brothers may redeem him:
\v 49 Either his uncle, or his uncle's son, may redeem him, or \add any\add* that is near of kin to him of his family may redeem him; or if he be able, he may redeem himself.
\v 50 And he shall reckon with him that bought him from the year that he was sold to him to the year of jubilee: and the price of his sale shall be according to the number of years, according to the time of an hired servant shall it be with him.
\v 51 If \add there be\add* yet many years \add behind\add*, according to them he shall give again the price of his redemption out of the money that he was bought for.
\v 52 And if there remain but few years to the year of jubilee, then he shall count with him, \add and\add* according to his years shall he give him again the price of his redemption.
\v 53 \add And\add* as a yearly hired servant shall he be with him: \add and the other\add* shall not rule with rigor over him in your sight.
\v 54 And if he be not redeemed in these \add years\add*, then he shall go out in the year of jubilee, \add both\add* he, and his children with him.
\v 55 For to me the children of Israel \add are\add* servants; they \add are\add* my servants whom I brought forth out of the land of Egypt: I \add am\add* the LORD your God.
\c 26
\p \v 1 You shall make you no idols nor graven image, neither raise you up a standing image, neither shall you set up \add any\add* image of stone in your land, to bow down to it: for I \add am\add* the LORD your God.
\v 2 You shall keep my sabbaths, and reverence my sanctuary: I \add am\add* the LORD.
\v 3 If you walk in my statutes, and keep my commandments, and do them;
\v 4 Then I will give you rain in due season, and the land shall yield her increase, and the trees of the field shall yield their fruit.
\v 5 And your threshing shall reach to the vintage, and the vintage shall reach to the sowing time: and you shall eat your bread to the full, and dwell in your land safely.
\v 6 And I will give peace in the land, and you shall lie down, and none shall make \add you\add* afraid: and I will rid evil beasts out of the land, neither shall the sword go through your land.
\v 7 And you shall chase your enemies, and they shall fall before you by the sword.
\v 8 And five of you shall chase an hundred, and an hundred of you shall put ten thousand to flight: and your enemies shall fall before you by the sword.
\v 9 For I will have respect to you, and make you fruitful, and multiply you, and establish my covenant with you.
\v 10 And you shall eat old store, and bring forth the old because of the new.
\v 11 And I set my tabernacle among you: and my soul shall not abhor you.
\v 12 And I will walk among you, and will be your God, and you shall be my people.
\v 13 I \add am\add* the LORD your God, which brought you forth out of the land of Egypt, that you should not be their slaves; and I have broken the bands of your yoke, and made you go upright.
\v 14 But if you will not listen to me, and will not do all these commandments;
\v 15 And if you shall despise my statutes, or if your soul abhor my judgments, so that you will not do all my commandments, \add but\add* that you break my covenant:
\v 16 I also will do this to you; I will even appoint over you terror, consumption, and the burning ague, that shall consume the eyes, and cause sorrow of heart: and you shall sow your seed in vain, for your enemies shall eat it.
\v 17 And I will set my face against you, and you shall be slain before your enemies: they that hate you shall reign over you; and you shall flee when none pursues you.
\v 18 And if you will not yet for all this listen to me, then I will punish you seven times more for your sins.
\v 19 And I will break the pride of your power; and I will make your heaven as iron, and your earth as brass:
\v 20 And your strength shall be spent in vain: for your land shall not yield her increase, neither shall the trees of the land yield their fruits.
\v 21 And if you walk contrary to me, and will not listen to me; I will bring seven times more plagues on you according to your sins.
\v 22 I will also send wild beasts among you, which shall rob you of your children, and destroy your cattle, and make you few in number; and your \add high\add* ways shall be desolate.
\v 23 And if you will not be reformed by me by these things, but will walk contrary to me;
\v 24 Then will I also walk contrary to you, and will punish you yet seven times for your sins.
\v 25 And I will bring a sword on you, that shall avenge the quarrel of \add my\add* covenant: and when you are gathered together within your cities, I will send the pestilence among you; and you shall be delivered into the hand of the enemy.
\v 26 \add And\add* when I have broken the staff of your bread, ten women shall bake your bread in one oven, and they shall deliver \add you\add* your bread again by weight: and you shall eat, and not be satisfied.
\v 27 And if you will not for all this listen to me, but walk contrary to me;
\v 28 Then I will walk contrary to you also in fury; and I, even I, will chastise you seven times for your sins.
\v 29 And you shall eat the flesh of your sons, and the flesh of your daughters shall you eat.
\v 30 And I will destroy your high places, and cut down your images, and cast your carcasses on the carcasses of your idols, and my soul shall abhor you.
\v 31 And I will make your cities waste, and bring your sanctuaries to desolation, and I will not smell the smell of your sweet odors.
\v 32 And I will bring the land into desolation: and your enemies which dwell therein shall be astonished at it.
\v 33 And I will scatter you among the heathen, and will draw out a sword after you: and your land shall be desolate, and your cities waste.
\v 34 Then shall the land enjoy her sabbaths, as long as it lies desolate, and you \add be\add* in your enemies' land; \add even\add* then shall the land rest, and enjoy her sabbaths.
\v 35 As long as it lies desolate it shall rest; because it did not rest in your sabbaths, when you dwelled on it.
\v 36 And on them that are left \add alive\add* of you I will send a faintness into their hearts in the lands of their enemies; and the sound of a shaken leaf shall chase them; and they shall flee, as fleeing from a sword; and they shall fall when none pursues.
\v 37 And they shall fall one on another, as it were before a sword, when none pursues: and you shall have no power to stand before your enemies.
\v 38 And you shall perish among the heathen, and the land of your enemies shall eat you up.
\v 39 And they that are left of you shall pine away in their iniquity in your enemies' lands; and also in the iniquities of their fathers shall they pine away with them.
\v 40 If they shall confess their iniquity, and the iniquity of their fathers, with their trespass which they trespassed against me, and that also they have walked contrary to me;
\v 41 And \add that\add* I also have walked contrary to them, and have brought them into the land of their enemies; if then their uncircumcised hearts be humbled, and they then accept of the punishment of their iniquity:
\v 42 Then will I remember my covenant with Jacob, and also my covenant with Isaac, and also my covenant with Abraham will I remember; and I will remember the land.
\v 43 The land also shall be left of them, and shall enjoy her sabbaths, while she lies desolate without them: and they shall accept of the punishment of their iniquity: because, even because they despised my judgments, and because their soul abhorred my statutes.
\v 44 And yet for all that, when they be in the land of their enemies, I will not cast them away, neither will I abhor them, to destroy them utterly, and to break my covenant with them: for I \add am\add* the LORD their God.
\v 45 But I will for their sakes remember the covenant of their ancestors, whom I brought forth out of the land of Egypt in the sight of the heathen, that I might be their God: I \add am\add* the LORD.
\v 46 These \add are\add* the statutes and judgments and laws, which the LORD made between him and the children of Israel in mount Sinai by the hand of Moses.
\c 27
\p \v 1 And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,
\v 2 Speak to the children of Israel, and say to them, When a man shall make a singular vow, the persons \add shall be\add* for the LORD by your estimation.
\v 3 And your estimation shall be of the male from twenty years old even to sixty years old, even your estimation shall be fifty shekels of silver, after the shekel of the sanctuary.
\v 4 And if it \add be\add* a female, then your estimation shall be thirty shekels.
\v 5 And if \add it be\add* from five years old even to twenty years old, then your estimation shall be of the male twenty shekels, and for the female ten shekels.
\v 6 And if \add it be\add* from a month old even to five years old, then your estimation shall be of the male five shekels of silver, and for the female your estimation \add shall be\add* three shekels of silver.
\v 7 And if \add it be\add* from sixty years old and above; if \add it be\add* a male, then your estimation shall be fifteen shekels, and for the female ten shekels.
\v 8 But if he be poorer than your estimation, then he shall present himself before the priest, and the priest shall value him; according to his ability that vowed shall the priest value him.
\v 9 And if \add it be\add* a beast, whereof men bring an offering to the LORD, all that \add any man\add* gives of such to the LORD shall be holy.
\v 10 He shall not alter it, nor change it, a good for a bad, or a bad for a good: and if he shall at all change beast for beast, then it and the exchange thereof shall be holy.
\v 11 And if \add it be\add* any unclean beast, of which they do not offer a sacrifice to the LORD, then he shall present the beast before the priest:
\v 12 And the priest shall value it, whether it be good or bad: as you value it, \add who are\add* the priest, so shall it be.
\v 13 But if he will at all redeem it, then he shall add a fifth \add part\add* thereof to your estimation.
\v 14 And when a man shall sanctify his house \add to be\add* holy to the LORD, then the priest shall estimate it, whether it be good or bad: as the priest shall estimate it, so shall it stand.
\v 15 And if he that sanctified it will redeem his house, then he shall add the fifth \add part\add* of the money of your estimation to it, and it shall be his.
\v 16 And if a man shall sanctify to the LORD \add some part\add* of a field of his possession, then your estimation shall be according to the seed thereof: an homer of barley seed \add shall be valued\add* at fifty shekels of silver.
\v 17 If he sanctify his field from the year of jubilee, according to your estimation it shall stand.
\v 18 But if he sanctify his field after the jubilee, then the priest shall reckon to him the money according to the years that remain, even to the year of the jubilee, and it shall be abated from your estimation.
\v 19 And if he that sanctified the field will in any wise redeem it, then he shall add the fifth \add part\add* of the money of your estimation to it, and it shall be assured to him.
\v 20 And if he will not redeem the field, or if he have sold the field to another man, it shall not be redeemed any more.
\v 21 But the field, when it goes out in the jubilee, shall be holy to the LORD, as a field devoted; the possession thereof shall be the priest's.
\v 22 And if \add a man\add* sanctify to the LORD a field which he has bought, which \add is\add* not of the fields of his possession;
\v 23 Then the priest shall reckon to him the worth of your estimation, \add even\add* to the year of the jubilee: and he shall give your estimation in that day, \add as\add* a holy thing to the LORD.
\v 24 In the year of the jubilee the field shall return to him of whom it was bought, \add even\add* to him to whom the possession of the land \add did belong\add*.
\v 25 And all your estimations shall be according to the shekel of the sanctuary: twenty gerahs shall be the shekel.
\v 26 Only the firstling of the beasts, which should be the LORD's firstling, no man shall sanctify it; whether \add it be\add* ox, or sheep: it \add is\add* the LORD's.
\v 27 And if \add it be\add* of an unclean beast, then he shall redeem \add it\add* according to your estimation, and shall add a fifth \add part\add* of it thereto: or if it be not redeemed, then it shall be sold according to your estimation.
\v 28 Notwithstanding no devoted thing, that a man shall devote to the LORD of all that he has, \add both\add* of man and beast, and of the field of his possession, shall be sold or redeemed: every devoted thing \add is\add* most holy to the LORD.
\v 29 None devoted, which shall be devoted of men, shall be redeemed; \add but\add* shall surely be put to death.
\v 30 And all the tithe of the land, \add whether\add* of the seed of the land, \add or\add* of the fruit of the tree, \add is\add* the LORD's: \add it is\add* holy to the LORD.
\v 31 And if a man will at all redeem \add ought\add* of his tithes, he shall add thereto the fifth \add part\add* thereof.
\v 32 And concerning the tithe of the herd, or of the flock, \add even\add* of whatever passes under the rod, the tenth shall be holy to the LORD.
\v 33 He shall not search whether it be good or bad, neither shall he change it: and if he change it at all, then both it and the change thereof shall be holy; it shall not be redeemed.
\v 34 These \add are\add* the commandments, which the LORD commanded Moses for the children of Israel in mount Sinai.
